{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018ymtGRkmTCYhEyvZSq8Rti","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (32.1KB). Full output saved to: /home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/05381da5-85e0-49d3-87e4-724cb00f5f8b/tool-results/b0300cqkq.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n# Web coverage atlas\n\nLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\nquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\nclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi (paren-wrapped LIKE), D04 path\ntraversal to `/run/huntress/objective.txt`, D05 unprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged \"isolated\ncallback\"), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08 session fixation, D09 CSRF (server-judged by\n`Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`), D10 unrestricted upload rendered by a `{{field}}` template preview. Since D05 every\ntarget is the same kit: `/api/clues` names `feature_route`, `secondary_route`/`render_route`/`preferences_route`,\n`current_role` + concept keys (`callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`, `session_hint`,\n`preview_guide`/`upload_policy`/`upload_shape`); the concept keys often spell the request shape in prose; stated\npolicies (\"txt only\", csrf_token) have been decorative. Routes return JSON errors naming the missing piece; success =\nJSON with `evidence: proof_...` (or the proof in a rendered page). Mastery = today's bug + 2 earlier lane-days (3\ntargets since D08), described only by today's prompt. Pace: D01-D03 cal. 19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21,\nD09-D10 cal. 22 (~2-3 lane-days per calendar day) -> priority 1 below = the bugs most likely in D11-D18.\nArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> access control -> XSS (reflected, stored) ->\nsession fixation -> CSRF -> upload. The client-side/session block looks closed; D10 turned server-side and already\nshowed a template engine evaluating `{{objective}}`, so next most likely: SSTI, OS command injection, SSRF, XXE,\nJWT / signed-cookie forgery, role tampering / mass assignment, then open redirect, DOM XSS, deserialization.\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05381da5-85e0-49d3-87e4-724cb00f5f8b","uuid":"638758f0-5065-4ab3-ae56-2576b59b222b","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:30:10.192Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Web coverage atlas\n\nLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\nquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\nclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi (paren-wrapped LIKE), D04 path\ntraversal to `/run/huntress/objective.txt`, D05 unprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged \"isolated\ncallback\"), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08 session fixation, D09 CSRF (server-judged by\n`Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`), D10 unrestricted upload rendered by a `{{field}}` template preview. Since D05 every\ntarget is the same kit: `/api/clues` names `feature_route`, `secondary_route`/`render_route`/`preferences_route`,\n`current_role` + concept keys (`callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`, `session_hint`,\n`preview_guide`/`upload_policy`/`upload_shape`); the concept keys often spell the request shape in prose; stated\npolicies (\"txt only\", csrf_token) have been decorative. Routes return JSON errors naming the missing piece; success =\nJSON with `evidence: proof_...` (or the proof in a rendered page). Mastery = today's bug + 2 earlier lane-days (3\ntargets since D08), described only by today's prompt. Pace: D01-D03 cal. 19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21,\nD09-D10 cal. 22 (~2-3 lane-days per calendar day) -> priority 1 below = the bugs most likely in D11-D18.\nArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> access control -> XSS (reflected, stored) ->\nsession fixation -> CSRF -> upload. The client-side/session block looks closed; D10 turned server-side and already\nshowed a template engine evaluating `{{objective}}`, so next most likely: SSTI, OS command injection, SSRF, XXE,\nJWT / signed-cookie forgery, role tampering / mass assignment, then open redirect, DOM XSS, deserialization.\nSnapshot 2026-10-22 (after D10). `lib/web/` now exists (`handlers/__init__.py`: `_KEY_MAP` clue-key regex ->\nhandler, `_HANDLERS` = only `session_fixation`, plus a `default` ladder; `lib/web/__init__.py` races handlers +\nevery earlier web day's `answer()`; `hctf web-harden`). `hctf prebuild` still has NO `web` lane and no `web:*` keys\nexist in `.run/prebuild-state.json` -> every prebuild gap below is still pending.\n\nStatus legend: `seen Dnn` = GM-confirmed lane-day (solver in `challenges/<cal-day>/web-*/solver/solve.py`).\n`gap` = nothing reusable in lib (D09 `csrf()` / D10 `upload()` live only in their day22 solve.py, not lib). Prebuilt web modules must be PURE (no `urllib.request`): bodies in -> request plan\n`[(method, path, headers, body)]` out; response in -> proof or next hints. The solver does the fetching.\n\n## Coverage table\n\n| # | concept | status | recognition cues | first move | likelihood next 3 cal. days |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | exposed backup / forced browsing via robots | seen D01 (Mastery x2) | robots `Disallow: /<word>-<hex>/`, \"crawler policy\", \"archive\" | robots -> index -> every link (depth 2) | done; Mastery |\n| 2 | IDOR (object-level authz) | seen D02 (compound) | \"Signed in as\", `/<things>/<id>`, `fetch('/api/<things>/'+id)` | foreign ids from `/api/history` | done; Mastery |\n| 3 | SQL injection (tautology) | seen D03 | search form, \"database\", \"one pointed question\" | `zz') OR 1=1 --` family | done; Mastery |\n| 4 | path traversal / LFI | seen D04 (compound x2) | `?doc=`/`?page=` filename value, \"mounted at /path\" | `../`*10 + prompt path | done; Mastery |\n| 5 | missing function-level authz (unlinked route) | seen D05 (D08 Mastery) | \"staff-only, just a sign\", clue `feature_route` | GET the clue route | done; Mastery |\n| 6 | role / privilege via client-controlled header, query or cookie | gap | `current_role: analyst` in every clue JSON, `role=` cookie | flip the value the app names | high |\n| 7 | JWT tampering (`alg:none`, leaked HS256 secret, kid/jku) | gap | 3 base64url parts in cookie / `Authorization` | decode; resign with `none` / leaked secret | high (session family after D08) |\n| 8 | signed-cookie / session forgery (Flask, Express `s:`, base64 JSON) | gap | `session=eyJ...`, `s%3A`, base64 JSON cookie | decode; re-sign with a leaked secret | high |\n| 9 | mass assignment / over-posting | gap | JSON profile update, `is_admin`/`role` in GET only | add `role:\"admin\"` to PUT/POST | high |\n| 10 | OS command injection | gap | \"ping\", \"lookup host\", \"diagnostics\" | `;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt`, `|`, `$()`, `%0a` | very high (server-side turn) |\n| 11 | SSTI | gap (D10 showed a `{{field}}` preview, benign lookup only) | \"template\", \"preview\", \"greeting\", `preview_guide`, `{{7*7}}`->49 | engine probe then file read | very high (D10 sequel) |\n| 12 | SSRF | gap | \"fetch URL\", \"preview link\", \"webhook\" | `http://127.0.0.1/<clue route>`, `file:///run/...` | high |\n| 13a | reflected XSS (server-judged callback) | seen D06 | \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\", clue `callback_nonce` | reflect `<script>fetch(cb?nonce)`, then GET cb with Sec-Fetch-* + Referer | done; Mastery |\n| 13b | stored XSS (moderator bot) | seen D07 | \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template` | store fetch(data)->POST receipt script; poll entry | done; Mastery |\n| 13c | DOM XSS (`location.hash`/`search` -> `innerHTML`/`eval`) | gap | inline JS reading location, \"client-side\", \"nothing reaches the server\" | scan sinks; bot visits `#payload` URL or callback check | high (XSS trilogy) |\n| 14 | default / leaked credentials login | gap | login form, creds in comment / backup / JS | use the leaked pair (no brute force) | med-high |\n| 15 | header-trust bypass (`X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1`, `X-Original-URL`) | gap | \"internal only\", \"localhost only\" | spoof the header the error names | med-high |\n| 16 | HTTP verb / method-override tampering | gap | 405/403 on GET, `_method=` | other methods + overrides | med |\n| 17 | path-normalisation authz bypass | gap | 403 on a named route | `/ADMIN`, `//admin`, `/admin;/`, `%2e` | med |\n| 18 | XXE | gap | XML/SVG/DOCX upload, `application/xml`, `upload_shape` naming xml | entity on `file:///run/huntress/objective.txt` | high (upload kit exists) |\n| 19 | NoSQL injection | gap | JSON login, \"MongoDB\" | `{\"$ne\":null}` | med |\n| 20 | unrestricted upload rendered server-side | seen D10 (Mastery w/ D01+D02) | \"upload form has standards. Low ones\", `upload_shape`, `render_route`, `preview_guide`, `upload_policy` | POST JSON `{filename:x.html, content:<p>{{objective}}</p>, content_type:text/html}` -> GET returned `path` | done; Mastery |\n| 20b | upload filter bypass / served-path traversal / stored SVG-HTML XSS | gap | policy actually enforced (`extension_not_allowed`, magic check), `../` in filename, uploads served raw | double ext, case, magic+type spoof, `../` filename, SVG script | med (D10 sequel) |\n| 21 | insecure deserialization | gap | cookie `gASV`/`Tzo`/`rO0`/`_$$ND_FUNC$$_` | tamper fields, then gadget | med-low |\n| 22 | exposed VCS / env / debug | gap | `/.git/HEAD` 200, `/.env`, DEBUG page | fetch, reconstruct, read secret | med |\n| 23 | GraphQL introspection / hidden field | gap | `/graphql`, `{\"data\":` | `__schema`, hidden fields | med |\n| 24a | CSRF (state change \"as someone else\") | seen D09 | \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\", \"forge one request\", `preferences_route`, form with hidden `csrf_token` | submit the form's external option with `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`/`Mode: navigate`/`Dest: document` + foreign Referer; read `/api/preferences` | done; Mastery |\n| 24e | CSRF sequels: token bound/checked, SameSite, JSON-body CSRF via bot | gap | token rejected when absent, `SameSite=Strict`, report-to-admin URL | token from own session, text/plain JSON form, GET-method downgrade, bot-delivered form | low-med |\n| 24b | open redirect (incl. OAuth `redirect_uri`) | gap | `?next=`/`?return=`/`redirect_uri`, \"after login\" | redirect to a clue route / `//host`; effect JSON | med-high |\n| 24c | CORS misconfig (reflected Origin + credentials) | gap | `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` echoing Origin, `-Credentials: true` | request with `Origin: null` / attacker; bot reads data | med |\n| 24d | clickjacking / framing | gap | no X-Frame-Options/CSP frame-ancestors, \"one click\" | effect likely judged server-side by headers | low |\n| 25 | prototype pollution (Node) | gap | JSON merge \"settings\", Node banner | `{\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}}` | med-low |\n| 26 | race condition / business logic | gap | shop / wallet / voucher, \"only once\" | parallel burst, negative values | med-low |\n| 27 | password-reset / predictable token / OTP | gap | \"forgot password\", token in response | read the leaked token; no brute force | med |\n| 28 | UNION / error / blind SQLi | gap | numeric id, DB errors | `ORDER BY`, `UNION SELECT`, boolean diff | med |\n| 29 | LFI filters | partial (D04 payload set) | \"not allowed\", `.php` appended | `....//`, double-encode, `pages/../`, wrappers | med |\n| 30 | request smuggling / cache poisoning / host header | gap | proxy + cache headers, reset links using Host | `X-Forwarded-Host`, CL/TE | low |\n| 31 | session fixation (planted id adopted by victim login) | seen D08 | \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\", clue `session_hint`, 400 `session_id_required` | `?sid=<hint>` on feature route -> cookie `arena_session=<hint>` on secondary | done; Mastery |\n| 32 | session hijack / weak session ids / logout not invalidating | gap | sequential or timestamp ids, ids leaked in URLs/logs/Referer | reuse a leaked id the app shows | med (D08 sequel) |\n| 33 | static web evidence (HAR, pcap, logs, web shell) | gap (never released) | `.har`, pcap magic, combined-log lines | jq / tshark / decode layers | low |\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\nFIRST 60 SECONDS ON ANY TARGET (cheap, in parallel, curl --max-time 20 -A 'Mozilla/5.0'):\n  GET /api/clues   -> feature_route / secondary_route / current_role + ONE concept key (see table below)\n  GET each clue route BARE: the JSON error names the missing piece (session_id_required, authenticated_login_required,\n      browser_callback_required, 401/403 = needs the victim's/admin's session)\n  GET /, /robots.txt, /openapi.json, /sitemap.xml -> links, forms, inline fetch('/api/..'), comments, Disallow\n  regex  proof_[0-9a-f]{32}  over EVERY body (JSON/base64/zip decoded). JSON `evidence` = answer.\n  410 {\"state\":\"completed\"} = attempt already solved; `preparing` = not ready, re-poll hctf status.\nPick routes by clue KEY (feature_/secondary_/*_data_route/*_template) and openapi paths, NEVER by the word in the\nvalue (callback|internal|status, messages|postcards are re-dealt per variant).\nMASTERY: 2-3 targets, prompt = today's bug only -> recon each target, run the hinted probe first, the rest staged.\n\nCLUE KEY / PROMPT CUE                                  -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST\nrobots Disallow, \"backup\", \"archive\"                   -> exposed backup     -> Disallow -> index -> .bak (depth 2)\n\"Signed in as\", /api/history ids                       -> IDOR               -> foreign id into the API template\nsearch box, \"database\"                                 -> SQLi               -> q=zz') OR 1=1 --   (+ ' \" )) # variants)\n?doc=/?page=, \"stay inside\", \"mounted at /path\"        -> traversal          -> ../ x10 + /run/huntress/objective.txt\nfeature_route only, \"staff-only, just a sign\"          -> unprotected route  -> GET it\ncallback_nonce, \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\"     -> reflected XSS      -> feature?q=<script>fetch('/cb?nonce=N')</script>, then\n      GET /cb?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, Sec-Fetch-Mode: cors, Sec-Fetch-Dest: empty,\n      Referer: <reflected URL>, Origin: <base>, X-Callback-Nonce: N   -> effect isolated_browser_callback\nmoderator_data_route + receipt_route_template,         -> stored XSS (bot)   -> POST /api/<noun> {\"message\":\"<script>..fetch(DATA,\n  \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\"                          {credentials:'include'}) -> POST RCPT(id from location.pathname)\n                                                            {evidence}</script>\"}; poll /<noun>/{id} and / for >=30 s\nsession_hint, \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\"      -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint> (sets arena_session=<hint>),\n                                                            then secondary with Cookie: arena_session=<hint>\npreferences_route, form + hidden csrf_token,           -> CSRF (D09)         -> GET / (arena_session), parse <form> on the page,\n  \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\"             submit the non-current external option with Sec-Fetch-Site:\n                                                            cross-site, Mode: navigate, Dest: document, Referer: foreign\n                                                            (token optional); then GET /api/preferences -> evidence\nupload_shape/render_route/preview_guide/upload_policy  -> upload (D10)       -> POST JSON {filename:\"n.html\",content:\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\n  \"upload form has standards. Low ones\"                     content_type:\"text/html\"} -> GET the returned path; policy is costume\ncurrent_role / role cookie / X-*-Role                  -> role tampering     -> set the named value to admin\neyJ..eyJ..sig in cookie/Authorization                 -> JWT                -> alg none / leaked secret, role claim\nlocation.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval in inline JS    -> DOM XSS            -> payload in #fragment; bot or callback check\n?next=/?return=/redirect_uri                           -> open redirect      -> point it at the clue route / //other-host\n\"ping\", \"host lookup\", \"diagnostics\"                  -> command injection  -> ;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt  (| $() ` %0a)\n\"template\", \"preview\", {{7*7}}=49                      -> SSTI               -> engine probe -> file read (D10 guide = where to inject)\n\"fetch URL\", \"webhook\", \"import\"                      -> SSRF               -> http://127.0.0.1/<clue route>, file:///run/...\n\"internal only\", \"localhost only\"                      -> header trust       -> X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (+ X-Original-URL)\nXML/SVG/DOCX upload                                    -> XXE                -> <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">\nA real victim browser exists (D07): anything \"the admin/reviewer/moderator visits\" can run your JS with their cookies;\nreceipts can land >12 s later. \"Browser\"/\"stranger\" checks without a bot (D06 same-origin, D09 cross-site) = send\nthe Sec-Fetch-Site/Mode/Dest + Referer/Origin matrix yourself -- one request each, try before anything heavier.\nNEW CLASS = write a key-matched handler in solve.py before TT: the generic lib.web race missed D09 and D10 (~40 s).\nBanners (\"Django\", \"Laravel\", \"Node.js\", \".php\") are costume; the title pun names the bug.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (~6-9 lane-days at the current pace). \"prebuild\" = pure python in a\nfuture `lib/web.py` (request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded\nbodies incl. a decoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built yet (no web prebuild lane); D09 CSRF and D10 upload gaps dropped (seen).\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: web is not a prebuild lane\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Still true after D10: hctf/prebuild.py LANES has no `web` entry and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys, so no prebuild gap below can drain. lib/web/ now exists (handlers/__init__.py `_KEY_MAP` clue-key regex -> `_HANDLERS`, `default` ladder; __init__.py races handlers + earlier days' answer()), so the lane's writable target is lib/web/handlers/ (one pure-ish handler per class) + tests/data/web_fixtures/. Owner of hctf/: add `web: {brief: prebuild_web, writable: (lib/web/handlers/, tests/data/web_fixtures/), targets: tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, gate: (tests/test_lane_fixtures.py,), regress_lane: web}`. Fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"clue-json-router\", \"concept\": \"map /api/clues keys + JSON error codes to the concept and the next request (rows 5, 13a, 13b, 31)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every target since D05 serves /api/clues {framework, feature_route, secondary_route, current_role, <concept key>}. Pure function: clues JSON (+ bare-route error bodies) -> concept + request plan. Known keys: session_hint (D08 fixation: GET feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with Cookie arena_session=<hint>; also try session_id/session/PHPSESSID names), callback_nonce (D06: reflect <script>fetch(secondary?nonce=N)</script> via ?q= on feature, then GET secondary?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin / Mode cors / Dest empty, Referer reflected URL, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce), moderator_data_route + receipt_route_template (D07 stored XSS payload builder with id from location.pathname), feature_route alone (D05 GET/POST). Known errors: session_id_required, authenticated_login_required, browser_callback_required, not_found. Select routes by KEY, never by the word in the value (callback|internal|status re-dealt). Unknown key -> return it as a hint for the worker. Fixtures: D05/D06/D08 clue bodies from the day-20/21 worker logs. Add D09: preferences_route (+ form with hidden csrf_token) -> CSRF handler (cross-site fetch-metadata submit, then GET /api/preferences); D10: upload_shape / render_route / preview_guide / upload_policy -> upload handler (POST JSON html with {{objective}}, GET returned path). Both handlers exist in challenges/day22/web-*/solver/solve.py (csrf(), upload()). Errors: signed_in_session_required, invalid_destination, method_not_allowed, file_not_found.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target without recursion or starvation\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 Mastery (3 targets) took ~15 min: racing every earlier solver on every target slowed the app 5 s -> 13 s, and day-21 solvers' fallback() imported each other (infinite recursion). Registry in lib/web.py: concept -> (detector over recon pages: home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json; request planner). Stage 1 = concepts the detectors hit (clue keys first), stage 2 = the rest, capped concurrency per host (~3). One flat registry replaces solvers importing each other. Fixture: recorded multi-target pair (D04 LFI + D07 board) with today's prompt for the wrong one.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/openapi/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Given fetched bodies keyed by path, return next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow, sitemap <loc>, openapi.json `paths` (fill {id} from submit responses), href/src/action, fetch('/..') literals, HTML-comment paths, every '/...' string in JSON, links on any directory index (depth 2), cap ~40, skip /assets. Parser: proof_[0-9a-f]{32} after JSON/base64/zip/gzip decoding. Fixtures: D01 robots -> index -> .json.bak, D07 openapi with /api/postcards + /postcards/{id}.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Session family opened on D08. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, backups, .env, JS, comments), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json). Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload.timestamp.sig with itsdangerous derive (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1) re-signed with a leaked secret. Escalate role/admin/sub (current_role analyst -> admin). No secret brute force beyond what the app leaks.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / JSON body / claim (rows 6, 9)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every clue JSON shows current_role: analyst. From recon: role field and values (current_role, role, is_admin, group, tier), app-set cookies, headers named in clues/errors. Plan: cookie role=<admin|staff|owner|higher listed value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User, ?role=, JSON role/is_admin on PUT/POST/PATCH to the profile route (mass assignment). Parser: effect+evidence JSON or proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"concept\": \"DOM XSS: client-side source -> sink (row 13c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Third XSS flavour after D06 reflected / D07 stored. Static scan of inline and linked JS for sources (location.hash/search/href, document.referrer, postMessage data, localStorage) flowing into sinks (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, document.write, eval, setTimeout(string), jQuery html()/$(), href/src assignment). Build the URL (#<img src=x onerror=fetch(cb?nonce)>, ?q=, javascript:) and deliver it the way the app expects: GET the callback ourselves with D06 fetch-metadata headers + Referer = crafted URL, or hand the URL to a report/bot endpoint and poll for the receipt.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-planner\", \"concept\": \"OS command injection to read the mounted proof (row 10)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For each flagged param (host, ip, target, domain, filename, cmd): separators ; | || && %0a $() backticks, with/without a valid prefix (127.0.0.1), reading the prompt path (default /run/huntress/objective.txt) via cat, `$(cat ...)` echoed, `${IFS}` space bypass. Parser: proof regex in response / tool output block.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ssti-engine-probe\", \"concept\": \"server-side template injection (row 11)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D10 preview already evaluated {{objective}} (a benign field lookup) -> a real SSTI day is the likeliest sequel. Arithmetic markers ({{7*7}}, ${7*7}, <%= 7*7 %>, #{7*7}, {{7*'7'}} -> 7777777 = Jinja2) -> engine; file-read payload per engine for the prompt path: Jinja2 cycler/lipsum/get_flashed_messages __globals__ os.popen, Twig source()/_self.env, ERB File.read, EJS/Handlebars/Nunjucks constructor chains, Freemarker ?new(). Also dump config (SECRET_KEY) to feed jwt-session-forge. Inject wherever the app renders user text: upload content (D10 shape), ?name=/?q= previews, profile fields; read the prompt path or an `objective`-style context var first ({{objective}}, {{config}}, {{self}}).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ssrf-planner\", \"concept\": \"server-side request forgery (row 12)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"URL-taking params (url, link, src, webhook, feed, image, callback). Plan: file:///run/huntress/objective.txt, http://127.0.0.1 / localhost / 0.0.0.0 / [::1] / 2130706433 / 127.1 + the clue routes (secondary_route is often the 'internal' one), named internal ports, 169.254.169.254 only if named, redirect and @-userinfo allowlist bypasses. Parser: proof regex in the preview body.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"open-redirect-planner\", \"concept\": \"open redirect / OAuth redirect_uri (row 24b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params next, return, returnTo, redirect, url, continue, redirect_uri, callback on login/logout/OAuth routes. Payloads: //evil, /\\\\evil, https:evil, %2F%2Fevil, /%09/evil, https://<base>@evil, javascript: (if the sink is client-side), plus the clue route as an internal target. Detect via Location header (don't follow) or meta-refresh/JS; when OAuth, leak the code/token to a clue route and replay it. Parser: effect JSON / proof.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"XML endpoints/uploads: in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64, XInclude, SVG / DOCX (zipfile) container builder carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode. D10 proved an upload kit with `upload_shape: POST JSON filename/content/content_type`; an XML/SVG sibling is the obvious sequel -> also try content_type application/xml / image/svg+xml through the same upload route and the preview path.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT; D07 Mastery's proof-2 fix could only be tested on a hand-built mock. Harness: log every target request/response during single/TT/Mastery into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"stopgate-503-already-solved\", \"concept\": \"harness: a 503 submit that landed leaves the stop gate closed\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D07 Mastery: submit returned HTTP 503 temporarily_unavailable though the GM registered CORRECT; the retry returned already_solved and stop_gate.py (counts only accepted/correct rows) never released. Owner of hctf/: after a 503, check op=status before retrying, and count already_solved for the owed attempt as done. Same for unverified live variants with expected.json {} (D08 Mastery).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"fetch-metadata-matrix\", \"concept\": \"server-judged 'browser' checks: Sec-Fetch-* / Referer / Origin matrix (rows 13a, 24a, 15)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D06 (same-origin callback) and D09 (cross-site CSRF) were both judged purely by request headers, no bot. Pure planner: given a route, a base URL and an optional 'from' page URL, emit header sets {Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin|same-site|cross-site|none} x {Mode: navigate|cors|no-cors} x {Dest: document|empty|iframe} with matching Referer (from-page / foreign https://evil.example/ / none) and Origin (base / foreign / null), ordered by the error/flag the app returned (browser_callback_required -> same-origin cors; changed_across_sites:false -> cross-site navigate). Parser: evidence/proof regex + boolean flags in the JSON. Fixtures: D06 callback and D09 /api/preferences bodies from day21/day22 logs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"port-day22-handlers\", \"concept\": \"lib/web handlers for CSRF and upload (rows 20, 24a) + dead-target short-circuit\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Both day22 TTs returned solver_incomplete after ~41 s because lib.web had no handler for the new class and ran targets serially. Owner of lib/: port csrf() (challenges/day22/web-forged-with-care/solver/solve.py; _KEY_MAP r'preferences|csrf') and upload() (challenges/day22/web-uploading-expectations/solver/solve.py; r'upload|render|preview') into lib/web/handlers; make lib.web.main thread targets, accept pre-fetched clues, and skip the 40 s race when GET base is non-2xx/3xx (410 completed).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"header-trust-verb-path-bypass\", \"concept\": \"IP/header trust, method override, path normalisation (rows 15-17)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route that 401/403/405s: X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP / X-Client-IP / True-Client-IP / Forwarded: for=127.0.0.1; X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL; methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS + X-HTTP-Method-Override / _method; path variants /ADMIN, /admin/, /admin/., //admin, /./admin, /admin;/, /%61dmin, /admin..;/, trailing ?/#. Stop at the first 200 with proof or effect.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cors-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"CORS reflected Origin with credentials (row 24c)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Request the clue data routes with Origin: https://evil.example, null, <base>.evil.example, sub.<base>; flag ACAO echoing + ACAC true. Exploit via the victim bot: stored/bot-visited script fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'}) from a cross-origin page and POST to the app's receipt route; or the app may judge it server-side by the Origin header (effect JSON).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"session-id-weakness\", \"concept\": \"session hijack: predictable / leaked / non-rotated session ids (row 32)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 sequel. Collect every session-like value the app reveals (Set-Cookie, clue hints, URLs, /api/history, logs pages, Referer leaks); detect structure (sequential int, timestamp, md5(user), base64 JSON); plan reuse of a leaked victim id as arena_session/sid cookie and a logout-then-reuse check. Never guess beyond values the app derives from data it shows.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"concept\": \"MongoDB-style operator injection (row 19)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JSON bodies: {\\\"$ne\\\":null}, {\\\"$gt\\\":\\\"\\\"}, {\\\"$regex\\\":\\\".*\\\"}; form username[$ne]=x; $where only when Mongo-flavoured. Field names from the form/JS. Parser: proof or an admin page with the returned session.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php within the capped recon list. Parser: .git loose objects (zlib) -> commit -> tree -> blob, .DS_Store names, Django DEBUG 404 URL list, .env secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sqli-union-blind\", \"concept\": \"UNION / error / boolean-blind SQLi (row 28)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"ORDER BY / NULL-count columns, UNION SELECT with table names from errors or sqlite_master / information_schema, marker-based string column, boolean-blind with a length-diff oracle (bounded, [0-9a-f_proof], 32 chars). Login bypass admin'--. SQLite/MySQL/Postgres dialects.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"graphql-introspection\", \"concept\": \"GraphQL schema leak / hidden field (row 23)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Introspection query, list fields, query hidden ones (proof, secret, evidence, note) and node(id) lookups (IDOR over GraphQL); field suggestions when introspection is off.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lfi-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"traversal filters / suffix / prefix rules (row 29)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Planner from D04's set: nested strip (....//, ..././), URL / double / overlong encodings,","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/05381da5-85e0-49d3-87e4-724cb00f5f8b/tool-results/b0300cqkq.txt","persistedOutputSize":32916},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018ymtGRkmTCYhEyvZSq8Rti","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
