{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018d8GnKYkSPYizoK36rZyYz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Web coverage atlas\n2\t\n3\tLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\n4\tquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\n5\tclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi (paren-wrapped LIKE), D04 path\n6\ttraversal to `/run/huntress/objective.txt`, D05 unprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged \"isolated\n7\tcallback\"), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08 session fixation, D09 CSRF (server-judged by\n8\t`Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`), D10 unrestricted upload rendered by a `{{field}}` template preview. Since D05 every\n9\ttarget is the same kit: `/api/clues` names `feature_route`, `secondary_route`/`render_route`/`preferences_route`,\n10\t`current_role` + concept keys (`callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`, `session_hint`,\n11\t`preview_guide`/`upload_policy`/`upload_shape`); the concept keys often spell the request shape in prose; stated\n12\tpolicies (\"txt only\", csrf_token) have been decorative. Routes return JSON errors naming the missing piece; success =\n13\tJSON with `evidence: proof_...` (or the proof in a rendered page). Mastery = today's bug + 2 earlier lane-days (3\n14\ttargets since D08), described only by today's prompt. Pace: D01-D03 cal. 19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21,\n15\tD09-D10 cal. 22 (~2-3 lane-days per calendar day) -> priority 1 below = the bugs most likely in D11-D18.\n16\tArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> access control -> XSS (reflected, stored) ->\n17\tsession fixation -> CSRF -> upload. The client-side/session block looks closed; D10 turned server-side and already\n18\tshowed a template engine evaluating `{{objective}}`, so next most likely: SSTI, OS command injection, SSRF, XXE,\n19\tJWT / signed-cookie forgery, role tampering / mass assignment, then open redirect, DOM XSS, deserialization.\n20\tSnapshot 2026-10-22 (after D10). `lib/web/` now exists (`handlers/__init__.py`: `_KEY_MAP` clue-key regex ->\n21\thandler, `_HANDLERS` = only `session_fixation`, plus a `default` ladder; `lib/web/__init__.py` races handlers +\n22\tevery earlier web day's `answer()`; `hctf web-harden`). `hctf prebuild` still has NO `web` lane and no `web:*` keys\n23\texist in `.run/prebuild-state.json` -> every prebuild gap below is still pending.\n24\t\n25\tStatus legend: `seen Dnn` = GM-confirmed lane-day (solver in `challenges/<cal-day>/web-*/solver/solve.py`).\n26\t`gap` = nothing reusable in lib (D09 `csrf()` / D10 `upload()` live only in their day22 solve.py, not lib). Prebuilt web modules must be PURE (no `urllib.request`): bodies in -> request plan\n27\t`[(method, path, headers, body)]` out; response in -> proof or next hints. The solver does the fetching.\n28\t\n29\t## Coverage table\n30\t\n31\t| # | concept | status | recognition cues | first move | likelihood next 3 cal. days |\n32\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n33\t| 1 | exposed backup / forced browsing via robots | seen D01 (Mastery x2) | robots `Disallow: /<word>-<hex>/`, \"crawler policy\", \"archive\" | robots -> index -> every link (depth 2) | done; Mastery |\n34\t| 2 | IDOR (object-level authz) | seen D02 (compound) | \"Signed in as\", `/<things>/<id>`, `fetch('/api/<things>/'+id)` | foreign ids from `/api/history` | done; Mastery |\n35\t| 3 | SQL injection (tautology) | seen D03 | search form, \"database\", \"one pointed question\" | `zz') OR 1=1 --` family | done; Mastery |\n36\t| 4 | path traversal / LFI | seen D04 (compound x2) | `?doc=`/`?page=` filename value, \"mounted at /path\" | `../`*10 + prompt path | done; Mastery |\n37\t| 5 | missing function-level authz (unlinked route) | seen D05 (D08 Mastery) | \"staff-only, just a sign\", clue `feature_route` |