{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKFoM7Yp6EMo4vorfKbx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HMqTz8cHKAimgQZGoxy1Df","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; T=$TMPDIR; cat > $T/build_gaps.py <<'EOF'\nimport json, sys\nT = sys.argv[1]\nold = json.loads(\"[\" + open(f\"{T}/gaps_old.txt\").read().rstrip().rstrip(\",\") + \"]\")\ng = {e[\"id\"]: e for e in old}\nfor k in (\"ssti-engine-probe\", \"port-day22-handlers\"):\n    g.pop(k)\ng[\"enable-web-prebuild-lane\"][\"detail\"] = (\"Still true after D13: hctf/prebuild.py LANES has no `web` entry (AUTO_LANES lists 5 lanes) and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys, so no prebuild gap below can drain. lib/web/handlers/ already loads per-day plugins `dayNN_*.py` exporting KEY_MAP + HANDLERS (D23 added three) -> the writable target is a new plugin file per gap, e.g. lib/web/handlers/prebuilt_<id>.py, + tests/data/web_fixtures/. Owner of hctf/: add `web: {brief: prebuild_web, writable: (lib/web/handlers/prebuilt_, tests/data/web_fixtures/), targets: tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, gate: (tests/test_lane_fixtures.py,), regress_lane: web, requires: (lib/web/handlers/__init__.py:_load_plugins,)}`. Fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\")\ng[\"codify-before-tt\"] = {\"id\": \"codify-before-tt\", \"concept\": \"harness: the class handler must exist before Time Trial starts\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\",\n  \"detail\": \"D23: D12 and D13 TT returned solver_incomplete (41 s, 12.9 s; solve.py a stub / no handler) because the orchestrator started TT ~1 min after single CORRECT while the codify worker was still writing lib/web/handlers/day23_*.py; the live worker then hand-solved. D11's single worker wrote its plugin BEFORE submitting -> TT CORRECT first try (solve 5.2 s). Owner of hctf/ + web skill: for web, gate TT start on the codify worker (or on solver-test passing the single case), and tell the single worker to write the plugin handler (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS, generic over param/field/route words) before `hctf submit`.\"}\ng[\"clue-json-router\"][\"concept\"] = \"map /api/clues keys + bare-route JSON errors + prompt verbs to the concept and the next request\"\ng[\"clue-json-router\"][\"detail\"] += (\" D11-D13 had NO concept key, so add a second stage: bare GET of each route -> `post_required` (405: POST sink -> second-order / mass-assignment / injection by body), `administrator_required` (403 on secondary: privilege bound elsewhere), empty `Rendered message <pre>` (render sink -> SSTI probe on ?template=), plus prompt verbs (\\\"binds whatever you hand it\\\" -> mass assignment, \\\"plant ... come back later\\\" -> second-order, \\\"evaluates everything\\\" -> SSTI). Plugins: lib/web/handlers/day23_web_template_temper.py, day23_web_ask_again_later.py, day23_web_posted_too_much.py.\")\ng[\"role-tamper-planner\"][\"concept\"] = \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / claim (row 6; body binding seen D13)\"\ng[\"role-tamper-planner\"][\"detail\"] = (\"Every clue JSON still shows current_role: analyst; D13 granted admin via JSON body binding (mass assignment, seen) -- the sibling forms are untested. From recon: role field and values (current_role, role, is_admin, group, tier), app-set cookies, headers named in clues/errors. Plan: cookie role=<admin|administrator|staff|owner|higher listed value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User / X-Admin: true, ?role=admin / ?admin=1, PATCH/PUT of the profile route with the D13 privilege key set. Then re-read the secondary route (403 administrator_required -> evidence). Parser: proof regex.\")\ng[\"sqli-union-blind\"][\"detail\"] = (\"D03 tautology and D12 second-order are seen. Remaining: ORDER BY / NULL-count columns, UNION SELECT with table names from errors or sqlite_master / information_schema, marker-based string column, boolean-blind with a length/row-count oracle (bounded alphabet [0-9a-f_proof], 32 chars), time-based (sleep/randomblob) only when nothing differs, login bypass admin'--. Payloads delivered as JSON body AND query/form (D12 bound JSON only). SQLite/MySQL/Postgres dialects. Title puns to expect: \\\"yes or no\\\", \\\"takes its time\\\", \\\"union\\\".\")\ng[\"deserialization-gadgets\"][\"priority\"] = 2\ng[\"logic-race-reset\"][\"priority\"] = 2\ng[\"prototype-pollution\"][\"detail\"] += \" D13 (NestJS mass assignment) makes the JSON-merge sibling more likely: after the pollution POST, GET secondary_route (administrator_required) and look for evidence.\"\nnew = [\n {\"id\": \"ssti-sandbox-escape\", \"concept\": \"SSTI sequels: filtered/sandboxed engine, file read, stored template (row 11b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"D11 rendered `{{objective}}` directly (context var) under a Spring Boot costume; `{{T(java.lang.Runtime)}}` printed a class, ${..}/*{..} stayed literal. A sequel may hide `objective` or filter `{{`. Planner: fingerprint by arithmetic family ({{7*7}}, ${7*7}, #{7*7}, <%= 7*7 %>, {{7*'7'}} -> 7777777 Jinja2 / 49 Twig), then per-engine reads of the prompt path: Jinja2 cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen / lipsum / request.application, Twig source() / _self.env, SpEL T(java.nio.file.Files).readString(T(java.nio.file.Path).of('/run/huntress/objective.txt')), Freemarker ?new() / ?api, ERB File.read, EJS/Nunjucks/Handlebars constructor chains, Thymeleaf __${..}__::. Filter bypasses: attr()/|join, hex/unicode, request.args indirection. Also plant in stored fields read later (row 37). Parser: proof regex in rendered body.\"},\n {\"id\": \"stored-second-order-generic\", \"concept\": \"plant now, read on another route: second-order for any class (row 37)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"D12 pattern generalised: feature_route = POST sink (`post_required`, `saved:true`), secondary_route = later reader. Planner takes a per-class payload list (SQLi ladder, SSTI `{{objective}}`/`${..}`, cmd `;cat <prompt path>`, XSS for a bot) and plants each as JSON (then form) in every common field (name,q,query,note,label,title,value,filter,search,term,report,display_name,bio,comment,message) in one body, re-GETs every reader route after EACH plant. Parser: proof regex only (D12 prints `effect` even when rows are empty).\"},\n {\"id\": \"type-juggling-auth\", \"concept\": \"loose comparison / JSON type confusion in auth or token checks (row 34)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"PHP/Laravel or Node costume with a token/PIN/password compare. JSON bodies with true, 0, \\\"0\\\", [], {}, null, \\\"0e1\\\" magic hashes, arrays where strings are expected (strcmp(array) == 0), numeric strings with whitespace. Field names from the form/clues. Parser: effect+evidence / proof.\"},\n {\"id\": \"bopla-field-read\", \"concept\": \"excessive data exposure / hidden-field read on API routes (row 36)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"API-family sibling of D13 (OWASP API3 read side). For each JSON route: query ?fields=*, ?include=all, ?expand=*, ?view=admin|full|debug, ?debug=1, Accept: application/vnd.api+json, and compare the key sets against the page; also scan list endpoints for objects with keys the HTML omits (secret, proof, note, internal). Parser: proof regex after JSON flattening.\"},\n {\"id\": \"http-param-pollution\", \"concept\": \"duplicate params / keys split between proxy and app (row 35)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"For a route whose check and action read the same param: a=safe&a=evil, a[]=..., JSON duplicate keys (first vs last wins), mixed query + body copies, ; separators. Order the planner by which copy the error names. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n]\nfor e in new: g[e[\"id\"]] = e\norder = [\"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"codify-before-tt\", \"cmd-injection-planner\", \"ssrf-planner\", \"xxe-payloads\",\n \"jwt-session-forge\", \