(name,q,query,note,label,title,value,filter,search,term,report,display_name,bio,comment,message) in one body, re-GETs every reader route after EACH plant. Parser: proof regex only (D12 prints `effect` even when rows are empty).\"},\n {\"id\": \"type-juggling-auth\", \"concept\": \"loose comparison / JSON type confusion in auth or token checks (row 34)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"PHP/Laravel or Node costume with a token/PIN/password compare. JSON bodies with true, 0, \\\"0\\\", [], {}, null, \\\"0e1\\\" magic hashes, arrays where strings are expected (strcmp(array) == 0), numeric strings with whitespace. Field names from the form/clues. Parser: effect+evidence / proof.\"},\n {\"id\": \"bopla-field-read\", \"concept\": \"excessive data exposure / hidden-field read on API routes (row 36)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"API-family sibling of D13 (OWASP API3 read side). For each JSON route: query ?fields=*, ?include=all, ?expand=*, ?view=admin|full|debug, ?debug=1, Accept: application/vnd.api+json, and compare the key sets against the page; also scan list endpoints for objects with keys the HTML omits (secret, proof, note, internal). Parser: proof regex after JSON flattening.\"},\n {\"id\": \"http-param-pollution\", \"concept\": \"duplicate params / keys split between proxy and app (row 35)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"For a route whose check and action read the same param: a=safe&a=evil, a[]=..., JSON duplicate keys (first vs last wins), mixed query + body copies, ; separators. Order the planner by which copy the error names. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n]\nfor e in new: g[e[\"id\"]] = e\norder = [\"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"codify-before-tt\", \"cmd-injection-planner\", \"ssrf-planner\", \"xxe-payloads\",\n \"jwt-session-forge\", \"role-tamper-planner\", \"open-redirect-planner\", \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"clue-json-router\",\n \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"fetch-metadata-matrix\", \"record-target-responses\",\n \"stopgate-503-already-solved\", \"prototype-pollution\", \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"deserialization-gadgets\",\n \"ssti-sandbox-escape\", \"stored-second-order-generic\", \"header-trust-verb-path-bypass\", \"sqli-union-blind\",\n \"logic-race-reset\", \"type-juggling-auth\", \"cors-misconfig-probe\", \"session-id-weakness\", \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\",\n \"graphql-introspection\", \"lfi-filter-bypass\", \"upload-filter-bypass\", \"headless-browser\", \"bopla-field-read\",\n \"http-param-pollution\", \"cache-host-header\"]\nassert set(order) == set(g), set(g) ^ set(order)\nout = [g[k] for k in order]\n# priorities must be non-decreasing in listed order\nprev = 0\nfor e in out:\n    assert e[\"priority\"] >= prev, e[\"id\"]; prev = e[\"priority\"]\nlines = \",\\n\".join(\"  \" + json.dumps({k: e[k] for k in (\"id\", \"concept\", \"priority\", \"action\", \"detail\")}, ensure_ascii=False) for e in out)\nopen(f\"{T}/gaps_new.txt\", \"w\").write(\"[\\n\" + lines + \"\\n]\\n```\\n\")\nprint(len(out), sum(1 for e in out if e[\"action\"] == \"prebuild\"))\nEOF\npython3 -I $T/build_gaps.py $T","description":"Build the re-ranked readiness gap JSON"}}}
