{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKFri2jJXXFd9q83jJsH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I updated both files and touched nothing else. Day23 released three web lane-days: D11 SSTI (\"Template Temper\"), D12 second-order SQLi (\"Ask Again Later\") and D13 mass assignment (\"Posted Too Much\"). All three finished CORRECT in every mode. Nothing was run or submitted.\n\n- **`reference/techniques/web.md`** (176 lines, now covers D01–D13): I added day entries for D11–D13 with the requests that worked and the time to CORRECT (59–105 s for the single solves). I also recorded the new GM `effect` spellings and error codes, and added variant axes for the SSTI parameter/delimiter, the second-order plant, the privilege keys and the JSON-vs-form body. Three new pitfalls:\n  - An `effect` value without the proof is not a solve.\n  - Send JSON bodies first: D12 ignored form fields.\n  - Write the handler before the single submit. D11 did and passed Time Trial first try; D12 and D13 didn't and Time Trial came back `solver_incomplete`.\n  \n  I also flagged that the docstring in the D12 handler (`lib/web/handlers/day23_web_ask_again_later.py`) is wrong: payloads ending in `--` won live in both the single and Time Trial runs. I didn't fix it because `lib/` is out of scope for me.\n- **`reference/coverage/web.md`**: SSTI, second-order SQLi and mass assignment are now marked seen D11/D12/D13. I added rows for possible follow-ons (SSTI sandbox escape, second-order versions of other bug classes, type juggling, parameter pollution, hidden-field reads). The recognition cues are 48 lines, with the three new cue lines included.\n- **Readiness gaps**: re-ranked; the JSON is valid with the same keys (34 entries, 29 of them `prebuild`). I dropped two that are done (the SSTI probe and porting the day22 handlers) and added five. Priority 1 is now command injection, SSRF, XXE, JWT, role via cookie/header, open redirect and D